WEBVTT

1
00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.452
Come on, Audrey.
Just tonight.

2
00:00:49.196 --> 00:00:50.754
I won't ask again,
I promise.

3
00:00:51.231 --> 00:00:54.598
How about you have
a nice glass of warm milk...

4
00:00:54.802 --> 00:00:57.362
...take a cold shower,
brush your teeth--

5
00:00:57.538 --> 00:01:00.507
- I already have a mommy.
- Oh, yeah.

6
00:01:01.875 --> 00:01:04.366
Why don't we ask her
if I should spend the night?

7
00:01:05.612 --> 00:01:06.909
How about we ask my dad?

8
00:01:07.181 --> 00:01:09.308
Come on, just tonight.

9
00:01:10.083 --> 00:01:11.778
I will see you later.

10
00:01:25.232 --> 00:01:26.995
Hey, yeah.

11
00:01:28.469 --> 00:01:30.300
She's gone.
Come on over.

12
00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.464
I do.

13
00:02:42.075 --> 00:02:43.099
Yes, I'm listening.

14
00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:44.334
I promise.

15
00:02:46.547 --> 00:02:48.538
Hey, homey, it's not
the end of the world.

16
00:02:48.715 --> 00:02:50.910
- You guys are killing me.
- We're killing you?

17
00:02:51.218 --> 00:02:52.845
I mean--
Oh, I'm sorry.

18
00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.578
All right, then.
I'm all in.

19
00:02:54.922 --> 00:02:55.946
Final hand,
final game.

20
00:02:56.123 --> 00:02:58.182
Put up or shut up,
all right?

21
00:02:58.559 --> 00:03:00.891
And to be clear,
the winner chooses the location.

22
00:03:01.194 --> 00:03:03.355
One dart, no ifs,
ands, or buts.

23
00:03:03.864 --> 00:03:05.559
All right, what are you doing?

24
00:03:05.766 --> 00:03:07.529
- All right.
- Now let me deal with this.

25
00:03:07.701 --> 00:03:10.135
- I call, I call.
- All right. Hey, listen, please.

26
00:03:11.271 --> 00:03:14.104
Did you just hang up on me?
What is going on over there?

27
00:03:14.274 --> 00:03:16.333
Are the guys over there?
Are you drinking?

28
00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:19.638
No, no, I am not
drinking right now.

29
00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.505
- Are you lying?
- No.

30
00:03:22.916 --> 00:03:24.281
Look, just tell me
the truth.

31
00:03:24.451 --> 00:03:25.713
No, I'm not, okay?

32
00:03:26.053 --> 00:03:28.317
Would you like
to come over and see?

33
00:03:28.488 --> 00:03:30.353
Yes, actually.
That'd be great.

34
00:03:31.692 --> 00:03:32.716
Yeah? No.

35
00:03:33.026 --> 00:03:34.050
- No?
- No, baby.

36
00:03:34.595 --> 00:03:36.586
What do we have
if we don't have trust?

37
00:03:36.797 --> 00:03:38.890
- What'd he say?
- "lf we don't have--"

38
00:03:39.366 --> 00:03:41.095
- Did you say that out loud?
- Just because I don't go to...

39
00:03:41.268 --> 00:03:42.462
...Bible school
doesn't make me a liar.

40
00:03:42.636 --> 00:03:44.103
No, but lying does.

41
00:03:44.538 --> 00:03:46.972
- Whatever, Caden.
- Audrey?

42
00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:48.801
- It is about time.
- No joke, man.

43
00:03:49.309 --> 00:03:52.642
Question. Why are we
throwing the dart?

44
00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:55.505
Why don't we Google
the 10 most exotic locations?

45
00:03:55.682 --> 00:03:57.479
Because one,
that would be typical.

46
00:03:57.718 --> 00:04:01.654
Two, we agreed the winner
chooses the location in one dart.

47
00:04:01.888 --> 00:04:03.583
So here we go.

48
00:04:04.925 --> 00:04:05.949
Oh, God.

49
00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.552
- Are you kidding me?
- No.

50
00:04:08.829 --> 00:04:10.660
We are not going to India.

51
00:04:10.897 --> 00:04:13.127
Bill, jump on the computer
and Google Hyderabad.

52
00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.528
Yes, master.

53
00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.763
- Hello, darling.
- She is on it.

54
00:04:19.239 --> 00:04:21.139
Okay, party's on, man.
I'm in.

55
00:04:22.376 --> 00:04:27.404
It says, "This is the crown jewel of
the country, home to the Taj Mahal."

56
00:04:30.484 --> 00:04:32.884
We're talking
one of the seven wonders of the world.

57
00:04:33.053 --> 00:04:36.250
Incredible beaches,
smoking hot red dress...

58
00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:38.082
- ...on those beaches...
- Red dress.

59
00:04:38.492 --> 00:04:41.484
...and we'd have more money there
than we have here?

60
00:04:42.195 --> 00:04:43.253
Damn.

61
00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:46.326
- Heck, yeah.
- Okay, good, good. Everybody good?

62
00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:47.967
So we'll talk tomorrow?

63
00:04:48.368 --> 00:04:50.928
I was getting ready to skinny-dip
in your infinity pool.

64
00:04:51.104 --> 00:04:53.265
- You weren't.
- Good night, drive safe, get out.

65
00:04:53.473 --> 00:04:55.168
All right, peace, man.

66
00:05:01.114 --> 00:05:04.948
Hi, baby, sorry,
just bad service.

67
00:05:05.585 --> 00:05:06.779
So what were you saying?

68
00:05:09.056 --> 00:05:10.648
A quiet night alone?

69
00:05:10.824 --> 00:05:12.382
What are you doing here?

70
00:05:12.626 --> 00:05:15.254
And when exactly did lying
become your second language?

71
00:05:15.829 --> 00:05:16.853
What?

72
00:05:18.131 --> 00:05:20.998
That's really what you're going with?
That's your answer?

73
00:05:21.301 --> 00:05:22.632
- Come on.
- "What"?

74
00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.695
When did you become
one of those guys?

75
00:05:25.872 --> 00:05:27.134
Why are you here again?

76
00:05:27.474 --> 00:05:29.533
You said you were alone.

77
00:05:29.943 --> 00:05:32.173
- I was.
- So I brought you a sundae.

78
00:05:33.146 --> 00:05:34.170
Liar.

79
00:05:34.347 --> 00:05:36.577
I'm sorry, okay?

80
00:05:36.917 --> 00:05:37.941
I'm sorry.

81
00:05:38.285 --> 00:05:40.446
Those guys don't
bring out the best in me.

82
00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:43.612
I know, I know.

83
00:05:44.758 --> 00:05:49.354
So will you stay a minute?

84
00:05:52.699 --> 00:05:54.030
Cheers.

85
00:05:57.804 --> 00:05:58.828
A minute.

86
00:06:01.675 --> 00:06:02.733
One minute.

87
00:06:13.487 --> 00:06:17.150
Yeah, that didn't really
seem like a great idea.

88
00:06:18.024 --> 00:06:20.584
I was just seeing
if it would light.

89
00:06:20.961 --> 00:06:23.361
- I don't even want it.
- Totally on purpose.

90
00:06:24.431 --> 00:06:26.296
You know, you're
becoming one of them.

91
00:06:28.001 --> 00:06:29.525
You're the only one
who says that.

92
00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:30.998
And who is them?

93
00:06:31.238 --> 00:06:33.229
You're the only one
who seems to think that.

94
00:06:33.406 --> 00:06:35.636
The reason I'm the only one
who says that is because...

95
00:06:35.842 --> 00:06:39.243
...you don't hang out with anyone
who cares enough to be honest with you.

96
00:06:39.412 --> 00:06:41.346
Thank you for the reminder.

97
00:06:41.548 --> 00:06:44.142
I mean, do you even think
about going to church anymore?

98
00:06:44.384 --> 00:06:46.113
- Audrey, please.
- Do you even miss it?

99
00:06:46.453 --> 00:06:50.389
Seriously, okay? Do you wanna know
why I don't go to church anymore?

100
00:06:50.557 --> 00:06:52.252
- Yeah, I do.
- Okay.

101
00:06:54.194 --> 00:06:56.059
I don't go to church
anymore because...

102
00:06:56.530 --> 00:07:00.261
...it puts me to sleep, okay?
It literally numbs my brain.

103
00:07:00.934 --> 00:07:02.834
All right? I've seen
the strings, okay?

104
00:07:03.036 --> 00:07:04.697
- You know what?
- They don't impress me.

105
00:07:04.871 --> 00:07:06.862
Everyone spends
eternity somewhere.

106
00:07:09.543 --> 00:07:12.740
Oh, no.
No, no, no.

107
00:07:14.247 --> 00:07:16.147
Not my girlfriend.

108
00:07:16.883 --> 00:07:23.288
Are you really resorting to that
bumper sticker T-shirt Christianity?

109
00:07:23.456 --> 00:07:25.617
"Everybody spends
eternity somewhere"?

110
00:07:26.493 --> 00:07:28.893
Not you.
Don't let them take you.

111
00:07:35.635 --> 00:07:36.897
Three-second rule, remember?

112
00:07:37.204 --> 00:07:38.501
You've gotta be kidding me.

113
00:07:38.738 --> 00:07:41.366
Your favorite rule. I'm not,
and you should know better.

114
00:07:41.575 --> 00:07:44.942
- That was silly two years ago.
- You don't have to be a jerk.

115
00:07:45.212 --> 00:07:48.010
- You don't have to act like a 12-year-old.
- You first.

116
00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:52.111
Honestly, Caden...

117
00:07:53.353 --> 00:07:55.082
...is this really
who you wanna be?

118
00:07:55.622 --> 00:07:57.954
Or should I be asking,
is this really who you are?

119
00:07:58.158 --> 00:08:00.956
I--
I'm cute.

120
00:08:01.228 --> 00:08:05.392
- Of course.
- And I am funny and sexy.

121
00:08:05.832 --> 00:08:08.733
And arrogant and entitled
and self-centered.

122
00:08:08.969 --> 00:08:12.200
- You forgot smart.
- Oh, so smart.

123
00:08:12.472 --> 00:08:14.064
What you
did right there proved it.

124
00:08:14.274 --> 00:08:15.502
- You're smart.
- Okay.

125
00:08:15.709 --> 00:08:17.438
Stop acting
like somebody you say you're not.

126
00:08:17.611 --> 00:08:19.238
Stop hanging out with my mother.

127
00:08:19.412 --> 00:08:20.572
Okay.

128
00:08:25.452 --> 00:08:27.181
Okay, okay, look.

129
00:08:27.888 --> 00:08:29.856
I'll make you
a deal, okay?

130
00:10:39.052 --> 00:10:40.076
Annikka!

131
00:11:57.297 --> 00:11:58.628
Not the prayer warriors!

132
00:11:59.332 --> 00:12:00.390
Hi, guys.

133
00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:03.468
- Hi.
- Are you guys still praying for me?

134
00:12:03.636 --> 00:12:05.228
- Always.
- Of course.

135
00:12:05.839 --> 00:12:08.399
- Thank you.
- We miss seeing you on Sundays.

136
00:12:08.641 --> 00:12:10.905
It'd be great to have
you back onstage, Caden.

137
00:12:11.144 --> 00:12:13.203
- Yeah?
- Did you get your guitar from Audrey?

138
00:12:13.379 --> 00:12:14.846
Yes, I did, Mother.

139
00:12:15.181 --> 00:12:17.547
Ladies, it's school.
It's the root of all evil.

140
00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:20.184
- Excuses, excuses.
- My schedule's hectic!

141
00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:22.183
We just miss
seeing you around.

142
00:12:22.355 --> 00:12:23.413
- Yeah, you know.
- Hi.

143
00:12:23.823 --> 00:12:25.222
- Hi, hi.
- Hey, baby.

144
00:12:26.259 --> 00:12:28.454
Nice car. Your father
out of town?

145
00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:31.797
- Bye.
- Thank you so much.

146
00:12:32.365 --> 00:12:34.196
- Coming through.
- Thank you.

147
00:12:34.467 --> 00:12:35.798
Is he cra--?

148
00:12:37.504 --> 00:12:39.438
By the way,
Dad is great.

149
00:12:39.906 --> 00:12:41.305
Could you be nice?

150
00:12:42.075 --> 00:12:43.235
Always.

151
00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:45.405
Mom, I'm hungry.
Do we have food?

152
00:12:45.612 --> 00:12:47.739
So, how is Audrey doing?

153
00:12:47.914 --> 00:12:51.008
I don't know, you tell me.
I'm sure you already know the answer.

154
00:12:51.184 --> 00:12:54.051
She just asked me
to pray for her, that's all.

155
00:12:54.487 --> 00:12:56.751
Mom, really?

156
00:12:57.690 --> 00:12:59.214
Stay out of my business.

157
00:13:00.293 --> 00:13:01.851
Just let it go.
Let it go.

158
00:13:02.328 --> 00:13:03.693
Mom, food, please.

159
00:13:03.963 --> 00:13:06.329
- Hey, do not be like that.
- I'm kidding.

160
00:13:06.733 --> 00:13:08.894
- Do not be like that.
- I'm just kidding.

161
00:13:09.068 --> 00:13:11.093
- Sandwiches?
- Yeah.

162
00:13:11.304 --> 00:13:12.498
So, how's
your life, kiddo?

163
00:13:12.805 --> 00:13:14.136
You get that job yet?

164
00:13:14.874 --> 00:13:18.173
Life? Life is good.
Thanks.

165
00:13:18.878 --> 00:13:20.812
The job?
No.

166
00:13:21.114 --> 00:13:23.912
I've been too busy
planning my trip to India.

167
00:13:25.652 --> 00:13:26.949
- India?
- Yeah.

168
00:13:27.220 --> 00:13:28.778
No, I don't--

169
00:13:29.055 --> 00:13:31.546
I don't think so. You made
a promise to your mother...

170
00:13:31.724 --> 00:13:33.521
...you were getting a job this summer.

171
00:13:33.693 --> 00:13:35.593
Be your own man
and take on responsibilities.

172
00:13:35.795 --> 00:13:38.229
- You remember any of that?
- Yeah.

173
00:13:38.398 --> 00:13:39.990
I don't know if you misunderstood.

174
00:13:40.166 --> 00:13:42.862
I'm not asking you
because I don't need your permission.

175
00:13:43.136 --> 00:13:45.070
I need hers.
Mom, India.

176
00:13:46.372 --> 00:13:48.465
You know what?
I think India's great.

177
00:13:48.741 --> 00:13:50.072
- What?
- Exactly.

178
00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:52.503
- It's great.
- Now I don't have to lie to Dad.

179
00:13:53.012 --> 00:13:55.276
I'm kidding, I'm kidding.
So, you're in?

180
00:13:55.448 --> 00:13:58.076
That depends.
You have to define "in."

181
00:13:59.052 --> 00:14:01.145
Please, please,
please define "in."

182
00:14:01.354 --> 00:14:02.981
All right, well.

183
00:14:03.223 --> 00:14:05.521
Dad said that you'd have to
sign off on the trip.

184
00:14:06.526 --> 00:14:08.687
Don't worry,
you don't have to foot the bill.

185
00:14:08.861 --> 00:14:10.021
Hey, come back here.

186
00:14:10.196 --> 00:14:12.289
I want to be very clear about something.

187
00:14:12.465 --> 00:14:14.456
This promise to your mother
to get a job.

188
00:14:14.634 --> 00:14:17.228
That promise doesn't mean anything,
is that right?

189
00:14:17.403 --> 00:14:19.303
Where are
you guys headed to in India?

190
00:14:19.472 --> 00:14:21.667
Look, Mom, we're going
to Goa, Agra...

191
00:14:21.908 --> 00:14:25.537
...Taj Mahal, Hyderabad,
which is the pearl capital of India.

192
00:14:26.879 --> 00:14:27.903
I'll get you pearls.

193
00:14:28.581 --> 00:14:29.741
"I'll get you pearls."

194
00:14:29.983 --> 00:14:32.008
And, Luke,
by the way, yes.

195
00:14:32.552 --> 00:14:34.611
Promising my mother
means everything to me.

196
00:14:34.821 --> 00:14:38.154
So, Mom, I will get
a job when I get back.

197
00:14:38.524 --> 00:14:39.548
Please?

198
00:14:41.394 --> 00:14:42.759
Yes, yes.

199
00:14:43.196 --> 00:14:44.754
- Yes?
- Yes, you have our blessing.

200
00:14:45.031 --> 00:14:46.896
Yes, thank you!

201
00:14:48.268 --> 00:14:49.599
Thanks for the sandwich.

202
00:14:50.503 --> 00:14:51.527
Thanks, Luke!

203
00:14:51.704 --> 00:14:53.763
Do you mind telling me
what just happened?

204
00:14:54.173 --> 00:14:56.641
Yeah, I mean,
haven't we been praying...

205
00:14:56.843 --> 00:14:59.038
...God would get hold
of him and shake him up?

206
00:14:59.212 --> 00:15:01.203
Yeah, yes, yes,
but India, really?

207
00:15:01.714 --> 00:15:03.272
- India.
- Yeah.

208
00:15:04.984 --> 00:15:06.008
Really?

209
00:15:06.185 --> 00:15:08.745
You never know. Really.

210
00:15:43.523 --> 00:15:45.013
Nice try, Mom.

211
00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:02.264
All right.

212
00:17:47.547 --> 00:17:49.538
- Yeah.
- Where the ladies at?

213
00:17:49.749 --> 00:17:51.910
We are in India, right?
Is that where we are?

214
00:17:52.084 --> 00:17:53.676
- It's English, okay?
- Hey, hold on!

215
00:17:53.986 --> 00:17:55.783
- Hello, my friend.
- What's your name?

216
00:18:03.229 --> 00:18:04.253
Hey, open the door!

217
00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:06.823
Call her.
She probably misses you.

218
00:18:07.033 --> 00:18:08.466
Hey, wait, wait, wait.

219
00:18:08.768 --> 00:18:10.497
- Do you think he's--
- Just a little bit.

220
00:18:10.703 --> 00:18:14.298
No, it's just misty. You're just misty.
We'll send her this.

221
00:18:14.474 --> 00:18:16.032
Do you want
to say something here?

222
00:18:16.209 --> 00:18:18.177
Yeah, it was a long flight.
I missed you.

223
00:18:18.511 --> 00:18:20.672
But look at Captain Serious
up in front here.

224
00:18:21.013 --> 00:18:23.311
Captain Serious, can we
have a little fun tonight?

225
00:18:23.583 --> 00:18:27.178
All right, yeah, shower, shave,
do whatever you guys do, wax.

226
00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:29.249
And then we are going
out to the club.

227
00:18:29.455 --> 00:18:30.979
Sounds like a deal.

228
00:18:31.657 --> 00:18:32.919
India!

229
00:18:33.226 --> 00:18:34.818
What?
Get inside the--

230
00:18:35.061 --> 00:18:36.528
Bring on the girls!

231
00:18:37.563 --> 00:18:40.396
Bozo. Who invited
this bozo?

232
00:19:45.865 --> 00:19:48.299
- All right, shots.
- Give me mine. Where's mine at?

233
00:19:48.467 --> 00:19:51.300
- All right.
- All right, here we go. 26 hours of flying.

234
00:19:51.470 --> 00:19:54.405
We are here, let's get
some action tonight.

235
00:19:54.774 --> 00:19:56.071
- Please.
- To us.

236
00:19:56.275 --> 00:20:00.837
Hey, hey, shot number one
of, let's say, 30? 40?

237
00:20:01.047 --> 00:20:02.344
- All right, done.
- Do it.

238
00:20:02.515 --> 00:20:03.539
Kick them back.

239
00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:08.851
Here's mine. Grab one.

240
00:20:09.021 --> 00:20:11.285
- We're good.
- Bottoms up.

241
00:20:11.591 --> 00:20:13.525
All right,
you and me, let's go.

242
00:20:13.726 --> 00:20:14.750
- Let's go.
- Come on!

243
00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:55.328
No, no, no.

244
00:20:56.402 --> 00:20:58.700
I gotta--
Gotta get some air.

245
00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:01.964
I'm not kidding.

246
00:21:23.262 --> 00:21:24.286
What?

247
00:21:24.864 --> 00:21:26.195
What are you looking at?

248
00:21:26.365 --> 00:21:28.799
Sir, please.

249
00:21:29.702 --> 00:21:31.067
I wasn't talking to you.

250
00:21:33.639 --> 00:21:34.663
Wait a minute.

251
00:21:37.576 --> 00:21:39.066
Haven't I seen you before?

252
00:21:42.381 --> 00:21:43.473
Man.

253
00:21:44.316 --> 00:21:47.012
We have homeless dudes
and beggars back at home...

254
00:21:47.286 --> 00:21:50.084
...but none of them
have a racket like this.

255
00:21:50.890 --> 00:21:53.017
You know, I mean,
you're using your own kid?

256
00:21:53.726 --> 00:21:55.216
Is she even
your own kid?

257
00:21:55.561 --> 00:21:57.893
I mean, I don't know
how they do it here.

258
00:21:58.431 --> 00:22:00.194
Please, money.

259
00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:02.495
Food. No home.

260
00:22:02.935 --> 00:22:04.197
You know English?

261
00:22:04.737 --> 00:22:07.069
I speak English, and,
well, that ain't English.

262
00:22:07.406 --> 00:22:08.896
Well....

263
00:22:16.282 --> 00:22:19.149
- I'll be nice this time.
- I'm saying I had a bad experience.

264
00:22:19.452 --> 00:22:21.283
I love that movie.

265
00:22:24.090 --> 00:22:26.524
Hey, hey, it's Caden.

266
00:22:27.126 --> 00:22:28.718
What's up, homey?

267
00:22:29.395 --> 00:22:30.692
What's up, buddy?

268
00:22:32.231 --> 00:22:33.892
What are you doing, man?

269
00:22:34.333 --> 00:22:35.857
Dude, this is not the night.

270
00:22:37.203 --> 00:22:38.465
The street corner.

271
00:22:40.906 --> 00:22:42.737
- What?
- The street corner.

272
00:22:43.209 --> 00:22:46.178
I saw this guy and this
puppet and this little girl.

273
00:22:46.345 --> 00:22:48.176
We saw them on the way
to the hotel...

274
00:22:48.380 --> 00:22:51.816
...and he's trying to tell me
they're hungry. Really? Really?

275
00:22:52.284 --> 00:22:54.479
You got a three-bedroom
in the hills, right?

276
00:22:54.820 --> 00:22:57.448
Know what? Wrap the clubs,
let's play poker at his house.

277
00:22:57.623 --> 00:22:59.215
- Hey, hey.
- What's the buy-in?

278
00:22:59.391 --> 00:23:00.415
You could play, too.

279
00:23:00.826 --> 00:23:02.487
- The party is inside.
- I got it.

280
00:23:02.661 --> 00:23:04.458
- Let's get our boogie on.
- Come on.

281
00:23:04.630 --> 00:23:06.655
- Let's go.
- Look, give me 15 minutes.

282
00:23:06.999 --> 00:23:08.864
Come back out.
Look at me, all of you.

283
00:23:09.068 --> 00:23:10.558
Do not leave me.

284
00:23:10.836 --> 00:23:13.737
I still got some Bollywood
dance moves going on.

285
00:23:14.173 --> 00:23:15.765
All right, ladies!

286
00:23:16.375 --> 00:23:18.172
Hey, what's your name?

287
00:23:18.911 --> 00:23:20.572
Lola, watch this.

288
00:24:17.570 --> 00:24:19.595
Hey, where's my watch?

289
00:24:20.039 --> 00:24:21.131
- Sir?
- Where's my watch?

290
00:24:21.640 --> 00:24:23.039
- We leave.
- No.

291
00:24:23.442 --> 00:24:24.466
- Yes.
- No, hey.

292
00:24:24.877 --> 00:24:25.901
Where's my watch?

293
00:24:26.245 --> 00:24:27.974
Sir, please.

294
00:24:29.682 --> 00:24:31.650
Give it back.
And how about my wallet?

295
00:24:33.152 --> 00:24:34.881
What's wrong with you?

296
00:24:40.159 --> 00:24:42.150
Sir, we need to go.

297
00:24:42.862 --> 00:24:43.886
Then go.

298
00:24:58.711 --> 00:25:00.338
Hey. Hey.

299
00:25:00.913 --> 00:25:02.505
Hey, where am l?

300
00:25:03.482 --> 00:25:05.006
Sir, not good place.

301
00:25:05.351 --> 00:25:07.342
No, no, no.
Where am l?

302
00:25:08.520 --> 00:25:11.045
I don't understand.
How did I get here?

303
00:25:11.690 --> 00:25:12.748
I'm all screwed up,
man.

304
00:25:13.025 --> 00:25:15.016
Sir, this okay.

305
00:25:16.996 --> 00:25:18.759
Sir, please, please.

306
00:25:19.732 --> 00:25:24.294
We're dying.
Annikka, she dying.

307
00:25:24.703 --> 00:25:26.728
Sir, I help you.
Why you no help?

308
00:25:27.406 --> 00:25:29.340
- I watch for you.
- You're being dramatic.

309
00:25:29.675 --> 00:25:30.937
Times are tough
everywhere.

310
00:25:31.243 --> 00:25:32.301
No, please.

311
00:25:32.478 --> 00:25:34.343
And stop pestering
people like me...

312
00:25:34.513 --> 00:25:36.003
...to give you
food and money.

313
00:25:36.682 --> 00:25:38.650
Get a job,
feed your own kid.

314
00:25:38.984 --> 00:25:41.748
It's not my deal, okay?
I don't have kids.

315
00:25:42.388 --> 00:25:44.948
I don't have a wife.
I don't have a girlfriend anymore.

316
00:25:45.124 --> 00:25:46.386
I have no idea
where I am.

317
00:25:47.059 --> 00:25:48.356
- Please.
- This isn't my deal.

318
00:25:48.661 --> 00:25:50.356
I'm sorry.

319
00:25:50.996 --> 00:25:53.726
Annikka not eaten
for three days.

320
00:25:54.266 --> 00:25:55.733
No food.
She dying.

321
00:25:56.001 --> 00:25:58.265
I help, why you no help?
Please, sir! Please.

322
00:25:59.238 --> 00:26:00.535
Listen, okay?

323
00:26:00.839 --> 00:26:02.363
You get me back
to my hotel.

324
00:26:02.775 --> 00:26:04.640
My hotel, all right?

325
00:26:04.910 --> 00:26:06.844
I'll help you,
I promise.

326
00:26:16.288 --> 00:26:18.051
Welcome back, sir.

327
00:26:18.724 --> 00:26:21.716
Please, sir.
Dalit not allowed.

328
00:26:23.329 --> 00:26:25.490
What do you mean, not allowed?
Of course you're allowed.

329
00:26:25.664 --> 00:26:26.961
Come on,
it'll be fine.

330
00:26:27.366 --> 00:26:29.800
- You're with me.
- Sir, they not let us.

331
00:26:30.402 --> 00:26:31.869
I feel like
I'm gonna get sick.

332
00:26:32.071 --> 00:26:33.868
Welcome back, sir.
Good to see you.

333
00:26:34.039 --> 00:26:35.063
They're okay, yeah?

334
00:26:35.607 --> 00:26:36.631
Who are they?

335
00:26:37.343 --> 00:26:38.401
It's okay for them?

336
00:26:38.577 --> 00:26:41.808
Trust me, no. You are not
supposed to be alone with them, actually.

337
00:26:41.981 --> 00:26:44.745
- They are not from here.
- You're joking, right?

338
00:26:44.917 --> 00:26:47.852
Please, Mr. Welles.
Please come inside. Please.

339
00:26:48.387 --> 00:26:50.685
Please, Mr. Welles.
Please come inside.

340
00:26:50.923 --> 00:26:52.015
I have to go inside.

341
00:26:52.191 --> 00:26:54.056
Sir, come back,
give us your help.

342
00:26:54.259 --> 00:26:56.159
- We wait.
- I'll come back, okay?

343
00:26:56.562 --> 00:26:58.052
- Please.
- I'll come back.

344
00:26:59.531 --> 00:27:01.021
Please, sir.
Please come inside.

345
00:27:01.233 --> 00:27:02.359
We wait.

346
00:27:06.205 --> 00:27:07.365
Sir, we wait.

347
00:27:10.175 --> 00:27:13.338
Take them out. Go from here.

348
00:27:23.989 --> 00:27:25.479
Buenos dias,
morning muffin!

349
00:27:26.692 --> 00:27:27.716
Hello!

350
00:27:30.029 --> 00:27:31.053
Turn the TV down.

351
00:27:31.463 --> 00:27:33.658
- Hey, come on.
- Come on, buddy.

352
00:27:34.133 --> 00:27:35.157
What time is it?

353
00:27:35.334 --> 00:27:37.894
You should be asking
what day it is, bro.

354
00:27:38.237 --> 00:27:40.899
You've been in bed
for the last two days.

355
00:27:41.073 --> 00:27:42.199
Tell me you're kidding.

356
00:27:42.441 --> 00:27:43.465
He's tired.

357
00:27:43.742 --> 00:27:46.404
We went to the management
to see if you were in a coma...

358
00:27:46.578 --> 00:27:48.773
...and we came and you were
passed out.

359
00:27:48.947 --> 00:27:51.575
We checked your pulse,
you were alive, and then we left.

360
00:27:51.750 --> 00:27:52.774
- You left?
- Yeah.

361
00:27:53.218 --> 00:27:54.651
- Seriously?
- Dude.

362
00:27:54.853 --> 00:27:56.821
- That's perfect.
- The Taj? Awesome.

363
00:27:57.056 --> 00:28:00.025
Taj Mahal.
Listen, we took a flight to Delhi...

364
00:28:00.259 --> 00:28:03.194
...then took a train to the Taj,
no joke, it was sick.

365
00:28:03.362 --> 00:28:05.262
Got back
this afternoon, homes.

366
00:28:07.132 --> 00:28:08.724
What's he doing?

367
00:28:09.468 --> 00:28:10.730
Please tell me you're kidding.

368
00:28:10.903 --> 00:28:12.837
No. It's like
flying to Vegas, dude.

369
00:28:14.206 --> 00:28:15.230
Oh, no.

370
00:28:15.607 --> 00:28:17.234
Sweetie, did we
hurt your feelings?

371
00:28:17.409 --> 00:28:18.808
No, no, you guys
are great.

372
00:28:20.079 --> 00:28:21.546
- Yeah, great.
- He's pouting.

373
00:28:21.847 --> 00:28:23.371
Don't give us
shit here, man.

374
00:28:23.549 --> 00:28:26.017
I'm so sorry,
pookie bear.

375
00:28:26.251 --> 00:28:28.446
We're not your mom, man.
Why are you upset?

376
00:28:28.821 --> 00:28:32.348
My mom wouldn't leave me in the street
passed out in a third-world country.

377
00:28:59.651 --> 00:29:01.551
We left you in
a super swank hotel, man.

378
00:29:02.054 --> 00:29:03.783
- A presidential suite.
- All right.

379
00:29:03.956 --> 00:29:06.447
- For two days.
- No big deal. It's all about the hotel.

380
00:29:06.625 --> 00:29:08.024
- We were drunk.
- Whatever.

381
00:29:08.327 --> 00:29:09.589
- Like, drunk.
- I'm leaving.

382
00:29:10.329 --> 00:29:13.059
I'd rather be sick
in my own bed at home than here alone.

383
00:29:13.332 --> 00:29:15.630
You are not alone, okay?
We are here for you.

384
00:29:15.968 --> 00:29:17.560
- Yeah.
- Yeah. What are friends for?

385
00:29:17.736 --> 00:29:19.704
Dude, I will--

386
00:29:21.573 --> 00:29:25.873
You're here for me,
once every few days or so.

387
00:29:26.044 --> 00:29:28.103
Dude, lighten up.
We're in India.

388
00:29:28.347 --> 00:29:29.371
We are in India.

389
00:29:29.581 --> 00:29:31.446
Doesn't matter. I'm calling my dad.

390
00:29:31.617 --> 00:29:34.643
I'm taking a first class
back to my own bed...

391
00:29:34.820 --> 00:29:37.050
...so you guys
need to leave. Get out.

392
00:29:37.890 --> 00:29:40.586
- Can you grab me a fresh beer, bro?
- Give me that apple.

393
00:29:40.759 --> 00:29:42.124
You guys, seriously.

394
00:29:44.830 --> 00:29:45.854
Come on.

395
00:29:46.498 --> 00:29:48.523
Have a nice day.
I'm glad you had fun.

396
00:29:48.867 --> 00:29:50.664
Out.
You have your own rooms.

397
00:29:50.836 --> 00:29:52.303
Wow, okay, well.

398
00:29:52.538 --> 00:29:54.335
Thanks for having
us over, sweetie pie.

399
00:29:54.873 --> 00:29:57.137
See you in the O.C.!

400
00:29:58.143 --> 00:30:00.475
I need a direct line
to America, please.

401
00:30:07.052 --> 00:30:08.076
Annikka!

402
00:30:09.288 --> 00:30:10.312
Annikka!

403
00:30:13.192 --> 00:30:14.216
Annikka!

404
00:30:14.626 --> 00:30:15.650
Annikka!

405
00:31:04.409 --> 00:31:06.070
Please stop.

406
00:31:06.778 --> 00:31:07.870
I'm coming.

407
00:31:14.353 --> 00:31:17.288
I already told you, okay?
This isn't my deal.

408
00:31:17.556 --> 00:31:20.024
I will not take responsibility
for your stupidity.

409
00:31:20.592 --> 00:31:22.059
Life is about choices, man.

410
00:31:22.761 --> 00:31:24.126
We're not friends.

411
00:31:24.763 --> 00:31:25.991
I don't need you.

412
00:31:26.498 --> 00:31:28.432
How many times
do I need to tell you?

413
00:31:28.734 --> 00:31:31.999
I learned a long time ago
that you are not to be trusted.

414
00:31:32.437 --> 00:31:34.371
You failed me
when I needed you most.

415
00:31:34.973 --> 00:31:37.032
Why would I ever choose
to trust you again?

416
00:31:49.821 --> 00:31:50.845
Hey!

417
00:31:51.089 --> 00:31:52.113
Hey!

418
00:31:52.291 --> 00:31:54.225
You can't just
leave her here!

419
00:32:37.502 --> 00:32:39.470
Sir, hurry.
We will miss the plane.

420
00:32:43.942 --> 00:32:45.500
Airport, please.

421
00:32:59.491 --> 00:33:01.550
- Oh, stop, stop, stop.
- No time.

422
00:33:01.827 --> 00:33:03.954
It's okay.
Give me a second.

423
00:33:20.212 --> 00:33:23.045
Sorry, sir. Boarding for that flight
closed 15 minutes past.

424
00:33:23.215 --> 00:33:24.239
Would you like....

425
00:33:40.399 --> 00:33:42.367
India, let's party!

426
00:33:42.667 --> 00:33:43.998
Get in the car, naked man!

427
00:33:44.169 --> 00:33:45.193
Bring on the girls!

428
00:33:45.771 --> 00:33:48.137
This guy's a stupid clown.

429
00:33:48.473 --> 00:33:49.565
Where are the women?

430
00:34:11.763 --> 00:34:13.594
You don't have to do it
one at a time.

431
00:34:18.437 --> 00:34:19.461
Hey, C.T., what's up?

432
00:34:19.805 --> 00:34:21.170
Hey, Liz.

433
00:34:21.406 --> 00:34:23.135
- Let me get Audrey.
- Thank you.

434
00:34:23.675 --> 00:34:26.143
Audrey, still
mad at Caden?

435
00:34:26.945 --> 00:34:28.606
It's none
of your business, really.

436
00:34:28.814 --> 00:34:31.146
He wants to talk to you,
so what do I tell him?

437
00:34:34.519 --> 00:34:36.282
Gotta go, C.T.
See you later.

438
00:34:36.688 --> 00:34:37.712
Thanks, Liz.

439
00:34:37.923 --> 00:34:39.584
Thanks for nothing, Liz.

440
00:34:39.991 --> 00:34:43.825
Well, maybe next time you'll
let me borrow your jeans, gosh.

441
00:34:44.029 --> 00:34:47.123
- Gosh, let her borrow your jeans.
- They don't even fit her.

442
00:34:47.365 --> 00:34:50.334
I gotta say, I didn't really
expect to hear from you...

443
00:34:50.602 --> 00:34:52.797
...after the way our
last conversation went.

444
00:34:53.371 --> 00:34:55.271
- What's up?
- Nothing good.

445
00:34:55.574 --> 00:34:58.600
I don't know,
I've been sick the whole trip.

446
00:34:59.478 --> 00:35:00.945
I'm sorry.

447
00:35:03.849 --> 00:35:06.784
I met this--
This guy.

448
00:35:07.586 --> 00:35:09.781
He came up to me
with his little girl...

449
00:35:09.988 --> 00:35:13.924
...and they were asking
for money for food.

450
00:35:14.092 --> 00:35:15.787
I don't know,
I kind of blew him off.

451
00:35:16.061 --> 00:35:20.259
And, I don't know, for some reason,
I didn't believe him.

452
00:35:21.132 --> 00:35:23.692
And his little girl
is really cute and really dirty.

453
00:35:23.969 --> 00:35:25.937
And, I don't know,
I didn't help them.

454
00:35:26.805 --> 00:35:28.796
Well, that
wasn't very nice.

455
00:35:29.207 --> 00:35:31.698
Oh, well, thank you
for stating the obvious.

456
00:35:32.777 --> 00:35:34.005
You're so helpful.

457
00:35:34.212 --> 00:35:36.806
Hey, you don't have to
get nasty with me.

458
00:35:37.148 --> 00:35:39.480
I was trying
to tell you something for once...

459
00:35:39.651 --> 00:35:41.983
...and you could have
just listened, you know?

460
00:35:44.222 --> 00:35:47.658
Anyway, I was just looking
at some pictures of them...

461
00:35:48.226 --> 00:35:51.423
...and I just have this really bad
feeling about it.

462
00:35:51.963 --> 00:35:52.987
I can't sleep.

463
00:35:53.598 --> 00:35:56.396
I told them I'd come back
and help them, but I didn't.

464
00:35:56.868 --> 00:35:57.926
And I should've.

465
00:35:59.304 --> 00:36:00.828
I feel like an idiot.

466
00:36:04.209 --> 00:36:05.642
What do you think of me?

467
00:36:06.077 --> 00:36:08.739
- Are you serious?
- What do you think of me?

468
00:36:09.681 --> 00:36:10.875
What do I think of you?

469
00:36:11.716 --> 00:36:13.843
Plain and simple.
I know what my mom thinks.

470
00:36:14.019 --> 00:36:16.544
Luke's easy,
he has to like me.

471
00:36:17.122 --> 00:36:20.717
My friends I could really
care less about right now.

472
00:36:21.960 --> 00:36:23.393
But you I can't sort out.

473
00:36:23.762 --> 00:36:26.128
So now I need
to be sorted out?

474
00:36:27.098 --> 00:36:28.156
Come on, Audrey.

475
00:36:28.333 --> 00:36:30.893
Please, for once, like,
you know what I mean.

476
00:36:32.003 --> 00:36:33.027
What do you think?

477
00:36:33.572 --> 00:36:34.664
Does it matter?

478
00:36:34.873 --> 00:36:37.967
Yes. What do you mean,
"Does it matter?" Of course it matters.

479
00:36:38.243 --> 00:36:41.872
I think that you ran away from God
when your parents got divorced...

480
00:36:42.614 --> 00:36:44.377
...and you haven't
found your way back.

481
00:36:45.050 --> 00:36:48.213
I think your mom is trying
to pray you back every day.

482
00:36:48.386 --> 00:36:50.115
And I think that Luke
loves you.

483
00:36:50.388 --> 00:36:52.856
Not because he has to,
because he wants to,

484
00:36:53.158 --> 00:36:55.820
And I think that you
can't see any of that right now.

485
00:36:57.228 --> 00:36:59.526
Wow, are you done?

486
00:36:59.965 --> 00:37:00.989
Whatever.

487
00:37:04.002 --> 00:37:05.765
That felt good
to get out, didn't it?

488
00:37:05.937 --> 00:37:07.336
As a matter of fact,
it did.

489
00:37:10.508 --> 00:37:14.069
Well, just to clarify that,
God ran from me first.

490
00:37:14.746 --> 00:37:16.111
Do you really believe that?

491
00:37:16.748 --> 00:37:18.238
Yeah, I do.

492
00:37:19.417 --> 00:37:21.851
Come on, Audrey,
do you even know how much...

493
00:37:22.053 --> 00:37:24.283
...I prayed
and got on my knees...

494
00:37:24.623 --> 00:37:27.820
...read the Bible,
did everything you're supposed to do...

495
00:37:28.627 --> 00:37:29.924
...and none of it mattered?

496
00:37:30.528 --> 00:37:31.552
Nothing changed.

497
00:37:32.330 --> 00:37:35.299
So because he didn't answer things
your way...

498
00:37:35.934 --> 00:37:38.198
...that means he didn't answer?

499
00:37:41.806 --> 00:37:42.830
Caden?

500
00:37:43.074 --> 00:37:44.098
Hello?

501
00:37:44.843 --> 00:37:45.867
I'm here.

502
00:37:49.314 --> 00:37:52.249
Look, it's getting late,
so I should probably go.

503
00:37:52.884 --> 00:37:53.908
Okay.

504
00:37:56.054 --> 00:37:57.078
I'll pray for you.

505
00:37:57.756 --> 00:37:58.780
Yeah?

506
00:37:59.958 --> 00:38:01.152
That'd be good.

507
00:38:04.529 --> 00:38:05.553
All right.

508
00:38:08.500 --> 00:38:09.797
I miss you.

509
00:38:11.770 --> 00:38:14.034
Okay, bye.

510
00:38:22.981 --> 00:38:24.642
- Hello?
- Mom?

511
00:38:24.949 --> 00:38:26.473
Hey, Caden.

512
00:38:28.420 --> 00:38:29.444
Hey.

513
00:38:31.022 --> 00:38:33.149
- Where's Mom?
- Oh, she just left.

514
00:38:33.425 --> 00:38:35.120
She's gonna be bummed
she missed you.

515
00:38:35.293 --> 00:38:37.056
How's it going?
Still in Hyderabad?

516
00:38:37.262 --> 00:38:41.562
Yeah, yeah, unfortunately,
I'm stuck here.

517
00:38:42.100 --> 00:38:43.294
Anything I can do for you?

518
00:38:43.535 --> 00:38:46.732
Yeah, help me
get out of here faster...

519
00:38:47.405 --> 00:38:49.464
...find Mom,
help me sleep.

520
00:38:49.674 --> 00:38:50.868
Any of those would help.

521
00:38:51.076 --> 00:38:52.737
Like I said,
your mom is not here.

522
00:38:52.944 --> 00:38:54.434
I'm not sure
when she'll be back.

523
00:38:54.779 --> 00:38:56.610
I wish I could help you
get home sooner.

524
00:38:56.848 --> 00:38:59.976
As far as sleeping,
I learned something a long time ago.

525
00:39:00.285 --> 00:39:02.515
lf my conscience
isn't clear, it haunts me.

526
00:39:02.687 --> 00:39:05.520
Keeps me up at night
until I've fixed whatever it is.

527
00:39:06.124 --> 00:39:08.024
Once I do, I can sleep
like a baby again.

528
00:39:08.493 --> 00:39:10.893
Maybe God's trying
to get your attention.

529
00:39:11.129 --> 00:39:12.153
What do you think?

530
00:39:12.697 --> 00:39:14.824
lf he is, can you tell him
to be a little nicer?

531
00:39:14.999 --> 00:39:18.560
Did you do something that keeps you
up at night, or was it God that did that?

532
00:39:19.771 --> 00:39:20.863
Point taken.

533
00:39:22.741 --> 00:39:25.505
What if I did do something...

534
00:39:26.010 --> 00:39:27.773
...and that's the reason
I can't sleep?

535
00:39:29.180 --> 00:39:31.307
What do I do if
I don't know how to fix it?

536
00:39:31.516 --> 00:39:34.781
I know you hear this from your mother,
probably from Audrey as well...

537
00:39:34.953 --> 00:39:38.081
...but why don't you pray?
God'll help you sort it out.

538
00:39:38.289 --> 00:39:40.655
He'll open doors, show you
a path. He always does.

539
00:39:41.192 --> 00:39:42.284
Not always.

540
00:39:42.527 --> 00:39:44.222
No, always.

541
00:39:44.796 --> 00:39:47.492
You might not be able to see it
right now, okay?

542
00:39:48.733 --> 00:39:49.757
Okay.

543
00:39:51.136 --> 00:39:52.160
Listen, I'm good.

544
00:39:52.771 --> 00:39:53.795
Thanks for the talk.

545
00:39:54.405 --> 00:39:55.429
Tell Mom to call.

546
00:40:01.045 --> 00:40:03.809
God, I can't find them.

547
00:40:03.982 --> 00:40:05.973
Okay, so if it's enough
that I tried...

548
00:40:06.284 --> 00:40:09.185
...then, please, let me
feel better about this.

549
00:40:11.556 --> 00:40:13.148
Okay, if you wanted
my attention--

550
00:40:19.864 --> 00:40:20.956
Please, sir.
Money, sir.

551
00:40:21.132 --> 00:40:22.156
Sir, sir,
money, sir?

552
00:40:24.235 --> 00:40:25.725
- There you go.
- Thank you, sir.

553
00:40:25.904 --> 00:40:26.928
You're welcome.

554
00:40:31.276 --> 00:40:34.473
Well, if you want my attention,
you've got it.

555
00:40:35.380 --> 00:40:36.540
lf it's enough--

556
00:40:38.883 --> 00:40:39.907
Really?

557
00:40:56.000 --> 00:40:57.024
Hey, hey.

558
00:40:57.268 --> 00:40:58.428
- Hey.
- No, no, no.

559
00:40:58.670 --> 00:41:00.831
No, it's okay, it's okay.
It's okay.

560
00:41:01.105 --> 00:41:02.129
Do you remember me?

561
00:41:03.508 --> 00:41:04.532
Do you remember me?

562
00:41:05.009 --> 00:41:06.909
Where's the little girl?

563
00:41:07.278 --> 00:41:10.441
- Where's the little girl you were with?
- Oh, gone.

564
00:41:11.449 --> 00:41:14.111
- What do you mean gone?
- Gone, sir.

565
00:41:14.285 --> 00:41:16.253
Whoa, what do you mean gone?

566
00:41:16.654 --> 00:41:18.019
Don't tell me she's dead.

567
00:41:18.189 --> 00:41:20.817
She-- She have
now good life.

568
00:41:21.426 --> 00:41:23.394
The education, best for her.

569
00:41:23.761 --> 00:41:25.626
It is best life.
Please.

570
00:41:26.130 --> 00:41:29.463
Wait a minute, you told me
you were dying.

571
00:41:29.901 --> 00:41:32.426
You told me that she was gonna die.
I don't understand.

572
00:41:32.837 --> 00:41:34.361
Sir, she would have.

573
00:41:37.709 --> 00:41:40.405
Well, okay,
just like that?

574
00:41:41.512 --> 00:41:43.070
All is well?

575
00:41:46.284 --> 00:41:47.308
You know what?

576
00:41:50.989 --> 00:41:53.082
Here, hey, hey.
Here.

577
00:41:54.259 --> 00:41:56.193
Better late
than never, right?

578
00:41:58.796 --> 00:42:00.593
What, is it not enough?

579
00:42:01.099 --> 00:42:02.566
Here.

580
00:42:07.405 --> 00:42:09.498
- Sir--
- No, no, no. It's for you.

581
00:42:23.721 --> 00:42:24.745
Stop.

582
00:42:26.791 --> 00:42:28.281
Where exactly
did she go?

583
00:42:28.559 --> 00:42:30.584
They not say.
They take.

584
00:42:31.429 --> 00:42:34.728
- Who wouldn't say?
- The man who buy her not say.

585
00:42:34.966 --> 00:42:36.126
Seriously.

586
00:42:37.936 --> 00:42:39.403
Please tell me you're kidding.

587
00:42:40.939 --> 00:42:43.271
No, sir, I told you,
it is best opportunity.

588
00:42:43.441 --> 00:42:45.602
School, job....

589
00:42:45.810 --> 00:42:46.834
Wait, wait, wait.

590
00:42:47.378 --> 00:42:49.505
You're telling me
that you sold your daughter?

591
00:42:52.016 --> 00:42:53.916
- The man--
- You sold your daughter.

592
00:42:54.152 --> 00:42:58.714
Sir, the man that got her
said this--

593
00:42:58.890 --> 00:43:00.949
- Yeah, you said that.
- Not easy for me, but--

594
00:43:01.225 --> 00:43:03.659
I just don't understand it.

595
00:43:03.861 --> 00:43:07.024
What kind of man buys a child?

596
00:43:07.799 --> 00:43:10.233
What kind of father
sells his own daughter?

597
00:43:10.401 --> 00:43:11.425
l....

598
00:43:12.971 --> 00:43:14.996
I no understand.
This is good.

599
00:43:16.174 --> 00:43:17.698
Can you show me
who bought your daughter?

600
00:43:17.875 --> 00:43:21.174
My cart, this my future.
This best for Annikka.

601
00:43:21.813 --> 00:43:23.678
- Please, sir--
- Annikka, that's her name?

602
00:43:24.215 --> 00:43:25.341
Annikka, daughter.

603
00:43:25.516 --> 00:43:27.609
That's your daughter's name?
The one you sold?

604
00:43:27.852 --> 00:43:31.913
Sir, if this best for her,
why you would not do that?

605
00:43:32.890 --> 00:43:35.586
Look, man, I don't--
I don't understand.

606
00:43:36.060 --> 00:43:38.756
No, sir,
this my cart, sir.

607
00:43:38.963 --> 00:43:41.090
No, no, no, stop.
Buy a new one.

608
00:43:42.033 --> 00:43:45.525
Okay, I'm not leaving until I see this is
what you say it is.

609
00:43:45.937 --> 00:43:48.531
Show me where you took her.
Take me where this happened.

610
00:43:48.706 --> 00:43:50.571
The little girl
he sold you yesterday.

611
00:43:51.909 --> 00:43:52.933
Yeah.

612
00:43:53.111 --> 00:43:55.375
Where's his daughter?
I need the girl. Annikka.

613
00:43:55.947 --> 00:43:57.073
She's gone.

614
00:43:58.516 --> 00:44:00.074
I'm just a supplier.
I don't know.

615
00:44:06.724 --> 00:44:09.591
Look, man,
this isn't right, okay?

616
00:44:09.894 --> 00:44:12.294
People don't
sell their kids, okay?

617
00:44:12.597 --> 00:44:13.757
They just don't.

618
00:44:14.032 --> 00:44:16.592
They get jobs or they
stay with friends.

619
00:44:16.834 --> 00:44:18.529
- Sir, go home.
- Wait here.

620
00:44:19.203 --> 00:44:21.330
- Wait here.
- Yeah, go home.

621
00:44:58.810 --> 00:45:00.744
Do you remember
exactly what...

622
00:45:01.079 --> 00:45:03.673
...that vendor guy said
about Annikka?

623
00:45:04.215 --> 00:45:08.049
She could work
with a wealthy family nearby...

624
00:45:09.087 --> 00:45:12.955
...get a good education
and food.

625
00:45:13.458 --> 00:45:15.449
Maybe even
her own bedroom?

626
00:45:16.627 --> 00:45:20.063
And that she could come
and visit you any time she wanted.

627
00:45:20.498 --> 00:45:22.523
This--
Yes, I told you.

628
00:45:23.668 --> 00:45:26.228
That's exactly
what they tell people.

629
00:45:29.273 --> 00:45:30.604
I knew this wasn't right.

630
00:45:30.842 --> 00:45:32.810
What you mean?

631
00:45:33.344 --> 00:45:35.244
What if what I just read
is true?

632
00:45:36.080 --> 00:45:37.104
What if....

633
00:45:37.315 --> 00:45:42.685
What if these little girls
that are sold into better lives...

634
00:45:43.421 --> 00:45:44.945
...that they
end up as slaves?

635
00:45:45.523 --> 00:45:47.650
Please, sir.
Don't tell me this.

636
00:45:49.360 --> 00:45:51.726
Please,
leave me alone.

637
00:45:53.297 --> 00:45:55.026
Look, man,
I'm only trying to help.

638
00:45:55.266 --> 00:45:56.699
How this help me?

639
00:45:58.503 --> 00:45:59.800
I trust she okay.

640
00:46:00.104 --> 00:46:01.128
You trust?

641
00:46:01.339 --> 00:46:04.103
All right, genius,
who do you trust?

642
00:46:05.977 --> 00:46:09.003
The guy who you give your daughter to
and gives you money?

643
00:46:09.213 --> 00:46:11.147
That's who you choose to trust?

644
00:46:16.754 --> 00:46:18.415
Let's just go back to the guy.

645
00:46:18.890 --> 00:46:21.154
We'll ask
in a different way.

646
00:46:25.796 --> 00:46:26.820
Okay?

647
00:46:30.268 --> 00:46:31.963
I heard that they are
taken to Goa...

648
00:46:32.136 --> 00:46:34.570
...from there to Bombay,
and then all over Asia.

649
00:46:39.010 --> 00:46:40.739
I can't believe
we're not flying.

650
00:46:41.312 --> 00:46:42.870
Why he tell you that--?

651
00:46:43.981 --> 00:46:47.417
Where my Annikka
if she not okay? She fine.

652
00:46:47.585 --> 00:46:48.609
I already told you.

653
00:46:48.920 --> 00:46:51.821
He didn't tell me where she is.
He told me where she might be.

654
00:46:51.989 --> 00:46:54.253
After I gave him
a handful of my money.

655
00:46:55.159 --> 00:46:56.717
There's a big difference.

656
00:47:18.182 --> 00:47:19.979
Now I lay me down to sleep.

657
00:47:20.384 --> 00:47:23.751
I pray my Lord
my peace to keep.

658
00:47:24.255 --> 00:47:26.348
lf I should cry
before I wake...

659
00:47:27.491 --> 00:47:32.451
...please take my fears
and bake me a cake.

660
00:47:36.000 --> 00:47:37.024
Dear God.

661
00:47:39.303 --> 00:47:41.362
I know it's been
a long time, but....

662
00:48:03.494 --> 00:48:04.518
Sir?

663
00:48:04.695 --> 00:48:05.719
Sir, where you go?

664
00:48:06.163 --> 00:48:08.290
He took my camera.
It's worth a lot of money.

665
00:48:08.833 --> 00:48:09.857
Wait!

666
00:48:15.273 --> 00:48:16.297
Sir!

667
00:48:36.260 --> 00:48:37.921
Sir, no, wait, sir!

668
00:48:38.095 --> 00:48:39.119
- No!
- Please, sir.

669
00:48:39.897 --> 00:48:42.764
- I'm gonna kill that guy!
- No, no, no, need-- Wait, sir!

670
00:48:43.634 --> 00:48:46.102
Please, sir.
Your bag here, sir.

671
00:48:51.742 --> 00:48:53.369
Sir, please, wait!

672
00:48:55.246 --> 00:48:56.270
It's fine.

673
00:49:06.791 --> 00:49:09.191
Well, the watch
my dad got me for graduation...

674
00:49:09.627 --> 00:49:11.288
...and the camera...

675
00:49:12.296 --> 00:49:14.389
...he and my mom got me
before they divorced.

676
00:49:15.866 --> 00:49:18.528
Our last Christmas
together as a family.

677
00:49:20.838 --> 00:49:22.135
These things mean a lot.

678
00:49:22.373 --> 00:49:23.533
Nothing worth this.

679
00:49:24.575 --> 00:49:25.599
Nothing.

680
00:49:26.944 --> 00:49:28.969
Well, this watch
is worth $20,000.

681
00:49:29.914 --> 00:49:31.905
That's a lot of lakhs.

682
00:49:33.651 --> 00:49:35.346
One lakh is--

683
00:49:36.520 --> 00:49:39.819
One lakh is rupees,
like five zeros.

684
00:49:40.624 --> 00:49:41.648
A lot.

685
00:49:42.259 --> 00:49:43.658
Okay, well, then.

686
00:49:44.395 --> 00:49:48.161
This camera is worth
about seven lakh.

687
00:49:49.100 --> 00:49:50.658
That's not that
much money, is it?

688
00:49:52.770 --> 00:49:56.103
Sir, nothing
worth the risk.

689
00:49:57.174 --> 00:49:59.506
But you risk more for life.

690
00:50:00.010 --> 00:50:02.035
Thank you. You came back.

691
00:50:03.948 --> 00:50:04.972
Thank you.

692
00:50:09.620 --> 00:50:12.316
Sir, you have faith?

693
00:50:13.891 --> 00:50:15.256
You talk to God?

694
00:50:19.363 --> 00:50:20.387
I'm Caden.

695
00:50:21.699 --> 00:50:22.723
Kiran.

696
00:50:26.070 --> 00:50:28.664
Sir, you have great faith.
I know.

697
00:50:29.640 --> 00:50:31.073
Once upon a time, maybe.

698
00:50:31.409 --> 00:50:35.004
No, sir, you came back.
This good faith.

699
00:50:54.698 --> 00:50:55.960
Sir, this not it.

700
00:50:57.334 --> 00:51:00.201
She with rich people
doing chores, the house clean.

701
00:51:00.971 --> 00:51:01.995
Sir, that's not--

702
00:51:03.174 --> 00:51:04.539
No, no, no,
don't panic.

703
00:51:05.976 --> 00:51:08.444
He said she might
be here, all right?

704
00:51:08.746 --> 00:51:11.237
So let's just hope
that he's lying.

705
00:51:13.284 --> 00:51:14.911
- A little girl.
- Little girl?

706
00:51:15.152 --> 00:51:18.315
- 7 or 8.
- So, come, then.

707
00:51:26.697 --> 00:51:28.324
Come, boss.
Go.

708
00:51:41.745 --> 00:51:42.769
Come.

709
00:52:07.838 --> 00:52:08.862
Come here.

710
00:52:35.065 --> 00:52:37.056
No, no, look, look, look.
I'm showing you.

711
00:52:39.570 --> 00:52:40.832
Here, come.
Follow me.

712
00:53:12.670 --> 00:53:14.797
What do you want?
Old girls? Young girls?

713
00:53:16.273 --> 00:53:17.297
Annikka here?

714
00:53:17.608 --> 00:53:18.632
No, who is he?

715
00:53:18.842 --> 00:53:20.309
He's just my guide.

716
00:53:20.711 --> 00:53:21.735
Annikka?

717
00:53:24.048 --> 00:53:25.345
Do you have little girls?

718
00:53:25.649 --> 00:53:26.673
I have many girls.

719
00:53:26.917 --> 00:53:28.509
We're looking
for a little girl.

720
00:53:30.421 --> 00:53:33.117
I have many girls.
Young girls, old girls.

721
00:53:34.124 --> 00:53:35.955
Give me one minute,
one minute.

722
00:53:38.562 --> 00:53:41.827
- Do you want to find your daughter?
- Listen, she's not there.

723
00:53:43.000 --> 00:53:44.024
This not possible.

724
00:53:45.269 --> 00:53:47.032
- You have two choices.
- Not possible!

725
00:53:47.204 --> 00:53:48.865
Listen to me!
You have two choices.

726
00:53:49.473 --> 00:53:51.771
I go in there
and you stay here...

727
00:53:51.976 --> 00:53:56.743
...or you can go and I will gladly go back
to the train and go back to the U.S.

728
00:53:56.981 --> 00:53:58.380
Okay?
It's up to you.

729
00:54:22.973 --> 00:54:24.270
My friend.

730
00:54:25.809 --> 00:54:27.071
How you doing?

731
00:54:27.578 --> 00:54:28.806
Welcome
to my heaven.

732
00:54:30.681 --> 00:54:32.444
Smells like flowers.

733
00:54:33.050 --> 00:54:34.381
Which one do you want?

734
00:54:36.487 --> 00:54:37.977
I want the one I showed you.

735
00:54:39.523 --> 00:54:41.252
I don't know.
She's not in here.

736
00:54:53.771 --> 00:54:54.795
What does it say?

737
00:54:56.674 --> 00:54:57.868
Ask your guide.

738
00:54:58.342 --> 00:54:59.366
He will tell you.

739
00:54:59.643 --> 00:55:01.440
You not buying?
I'm not bothered.

740
00:55:02.579 --> 00:55:03.603
Go.

741
00:55:09.219 --> 00:55:10.516
You deserve it!

742
00:55:11.021 --> 00:55:13.012
God, what I do?

743
00:55:15.225 --> 00:55:16.988
I can't read this.

744
00:55:30.441 --> 00:55:32.466
Audrey, hello?

745
00:55:37.281 --> 00:55:39.340
Audrey, hey,
it's me.

746
00:55:40.818 --> 00:55:43.013
I wish you would've
picked up.

747
00:55:45.989 --> 00:55:47.479
I can't....

748
00:55:50.561 --> 00:55:52.791
I don't even know
what to say right now.

749
00:55:56.300 --> 00:55:59.929
So I found the guy,
but not the little girl.

750
00:56:00.804 --> 00:56:02.066
He sold her.

751
00:56:23.360 --> 00:56:25.988
Come on, Audrey,
pick up, please.

752
00:56:29.199 --> 00:56:30.291
Caden?

753
00:56:31.668 --> 00:56:34.136
I just listened to your message
and I was praying.

754
00:56:34.705 --> 00:56:37.037
Yeah, well, after
what I've seen today...

755
00:56:37.207 --> 00:56:38.936
...Prayer seems like
a complete joke.

756
00:56:39.176 --> 00:56:41.838
I can't even find
the girl we're looking for...

757
00:56:42.880 --> 00:56:44.973
...but these little girls
and their faces....

758
00:56:45.215 --> 00:56:46.580
You have to trust in God.

759
00:56:46.917 --> 00:56:49.044
Sometimes we have
to be broken to be useful.

760
00:56:49.953 --> 00:56:51.147
That's brilliant,
Audrey.

761
00:56:51.722 --> 00:56:53.280
Completely brilliant.

762
00:56:53.924 --> 00:56:55.858
You know,
that's so you.

763
00:56:56.527 --> 00:56:58.552
The gospel according
to Audrey.

764
00:56:58.962 --> 00:57:01.453
Let me just tell you,
in my experiences with God...

765
00:57:01.899 --> 00:57:04.595
...l have zero reasons
to trust in him right now.

766
00:57:04.768 --> 00:57:07.328
Caden, you need to know
that God is with you...

767
00:57:07.638 --> 00:57:08.798
...and that he loves you.

768
00:57:09.339 --> 00:57:10.829
That isn't
the God I know, okay?

769
00:57:11.008 --> 00:57:13.374
The God I know
I prayed to every night...

770
00:57:13.544 --> 00:57:15.842
...and begged
for a response, okay?

771
00:57:16.079 --> 00:57:17.569
The silence
was deafening.

772
00:57:18.081 --> 00:57:20.572
I sat and watched my family
disintegrate, okay?

773
00:57:20.751 --> 00:57:21.911
This girl could be dead.

774
00:57:22.352 --> 00:57:23.376
You're not hearing me.

775
00:57:23.654 --> 00:57:26.214
And to be honest with you,
being dead would not be...

776
00:57:26.390 --> 00:57:28.358
...the worst thing,
after what I saw today.

777
00:57:28.525 --> 00:57:29.549
Sir.

778
00:57:30.828 --> 00:57:31.852
Not--
Not say that.

779
00:57:32.062 --> 00:57:33.825
- Caden?
- What if she is dead?

780
00:57:34.198 --> 00:57:35.756
What if this
can't be fixed?

781
00:57:36.233 --> 00:57:38.224
What if I've done
all I can do, Kiran?

782
00:57:38.569 --> 00:57:41.663
So what do you do,
just go to America? Disneyland?

783
00:57:41.872 --> 00:57:43.305
"Disneyland."

784
00:57:43.807 --> 00:57:46.173
- You don't get to judge me.
- Sir, please--

785
00:57:46.643 --> 00:57:48.941
You might've sold
your daughter into prostitution.

786
00:57:49.112 --> 00:57:51.444
- No, no, no, shut up!
- You cannot judge me!

787
00:57:52.182 --> 00:57:53.513
Sir!

788
00:57:59.723 --> 00:58:01.657
Oh, God.

789
00:58:05.863 --> 00:58:07.057
Sir.

790
00:58:09.600 --> 00:58:12.467
I'm not trying
to be mean, okay?

791
00:58:12.769 --> 00:58:13.793
But...

792
00:58:14.938 --> 00:58:16.803
...you stink, man.

793
00:58:18.775 --> 00:58:20.333
And now I stink.

794
00:58:21.612 --> 00:58:22.636
You need a shower.

795
00:58:23.113 --> 00:58:25.513
I need to shower.
You need everything...

796
00:58:26.450 --> 00:58:28.441
...starting with
new clothes.

797
00:58:34.591 --> 00:58:37.059
And how do you know
about Disneyland, anyway?

798
00:58:42.266 --> 00:58:44.496
These little girls,
they were offered to me.

799
00:58:45.235 --> 00:58:47.066
And they were, like,
7 or 8 years old.

800
00:58:47.237 --> 00:58:50.138
Caden, I can't even
understand that.

801
00:58:52.242 --> 00:58:55.575
It must be heartbreaking.

802
00:58:58.215 --> 00:59:00.115
I admire you
so much right now.

803
00:59:00.784 --> 00:59:03.309
I'm also realizing that...

804
00:59:04.187 --> 00:59:06.417
...l have a lot of growing up
to do myself.

805
00:59:07.391 --> 00:59:08.881
I want to make
a difference.

806
00:59:09.326 --> 00:59:13.285
I wanna be doing what you're doing
right now so badly...

807
00:59:13.563 --> 00:59:16.498
...but the truth is,
I'd probably pee my pants.

808
00:59:19.636 --> 00:59:22.935
I'd be so scared, Caden,
I'd run away.

809
00:59:23.540 --> 00:59:26.373
But like you said...

810
00:59:26.643 --> 00:59:29.612
...you are the one
there, okay?

811
00:59:29.846 --> 00:59:31.336
And you are not
running away.

812
00:59:31.548 --> 00:59:33.573
You are acting
as God's hands right now.

813
00:59:33.750 --> 00:59:35.650
You're being what the church
claims to be.

814
00:59:35.819 --> 00:59:37.719
But what if
she's dead, Audrey?

815
00:59:39.056 --> 00:59:40.080
It's possible.

816
00:59:42.326 --> 00:59:43.350
Maybe l....

817
00:59:44.995 --> 00:59:46.019
I don't even know.

818
00:59:46.463 --> 00:59:50.058
Listen to me,
that little girl needs you.

819
00:59:51.668 --> 00:59:52.999
She needs you,
Caden.

820
00:59:53.670 --> 00:59:55.137
She needs you
to find her.

821
00:59:55.739 --> 00:59:57.070
And her father...

822
00:59:57.441 --> 00:59:59.966
...he needs you to be strong
because he won't be.

823
01:00:01.011 --> 01:00:03.275
He believes in you
and so do I.

824
01:00:04.247 --> 01:00:07.580
I know that you are sick
of me saying things like this...

825
01:00:09.052 --> 01:00:10.246
...but God is watching.

826
01:00:11.722 --> 01:00:16.125
Whether you feel him or not,
he is there with you.

827
01:00:17.594 --> 01:00:19.152
He cares about you.

828
01:00:21.431 --> 01:00:24.025
More than
you could ever imagine.

829
01:00:39.883 --> 01:00:42.317
I wish I could
believe that!

830
01:01:27.297 --> 01:01:29.492
Hey, what's the matter?
Is something wrong?

831
01:01:29.666 --> 01:01:31.566
Why didn't he
help those people?

832
01:01:33.270 --> 01:01:34.294
What?

833
01:01:36.173 --> 01:01:37.868
Why didn't he
help those people?

834
01:01:39.576 --> 01:01:42.067
- And that little girl.
- Nobody's sorrier about that...

835
01:01:42.279 --> 01:01:43.871
...than he is
right now.

836
01:01:46.950 --> 01:01:49.714
Listen, why do you think
he's not answering his phone?

837
01:01:50.253 --> 01:01:52.721
He said the phone doesn't work
everywhere he is.

838
01:01:52.889 --> 01:01:54.720
He said that.
He's in India, sweetheart.

839
01:01:54.891 --> 01:01:56.119
It doesn't
work everywhere.

840
01:01:56.293 --> 01:01:58.158
Let's go to sleep.
Come on, sweetie.

841
01:02:00.797 --> 01:02:02.992
What--
What were you thinking?

842
01:02:03.700 --> 01:02:04.724
Wake up.

843
01:02:07.037 --> 01:02:08.902
What were you
thinking?

844
01:02:09.673 --> 01:02:10.697
What?

845
01:02:10.941 --> 01:02:12.704
You're always saying
you're the one...

846
01:02:12.876 --> 01:02:16.744
...that's responsible for our family
before God. What were you thinking?

847
01:02:17.080 --> 01:02:20.379
lf I don't know what you're thinking
and you keep making decisions...

848
01:02:20.617 --> 01:02:22.710
...without consulting
your husband first...

849
01:02:22.986 --> 01:02:24.749
...what am I supposed
to do with that?

850
01:02:24.921 --> 01:02:27.355
- It's kinda difficult.
- No, you just stood there.

851
01:02:27.557 --> 01:02:31.425
You didn't argue, you didn't disagree.
You just leaned on the counter.

852
01:02:31.595 --> 01:02:33.563
I had no idea.
You kept pulling my hand...

853
01:02:33.797 --> 01:02:35.458
...and stopping me
from speaking...

854
01:02:35.632 --> 01:02:38.066
...and you were looking at me
with those pretty eyes.

855
01:02:38.635 --> 01:02:42.036
Sweetheart, it's late.
Come on, let's go to bed. Come on.

856
01:02:46.143 --> 01:02:48.304
Okay, okay, okay,
I'm sorry.

857
01:02:48.678 --> 01:02:49.702
No.

858
01:02:49.880 --> 01:02:52.474
I know that you're scared.
I can see that you're scared.

859
01:02:53.650 --> 01:02:55.413
Something bad
is happening.

860
01:02:55.752 --> 01:02:59.051
You know what? Something bad is
happening and there's nothing I can do.

861
01:02:59.222 --> 01:03:00.985
- Hey, hey, hey.
- And you know what?

862
01:03:01.258 --> 01:03:02.520
I'm the one
that let him go,

863
01:03:02.726 --> 01:03:06.025
I'm the one that wanted this to happen
and for God to shake him up.

864
01:03:06.830 --> 01:03:10.288
You're the one who thought it was
a good idea, and I trust your judgment.

865
01:03:10.534 --> 01:03:14.129
You have very good judgment, okay?
And if you look at it...

866
01:03:14.337 --> 01:03:16.498
...you can see that God's hand
is all over it.

867
01:03:17.207 --> 01:03:18.231
It's everywhere.

868
01:03:20.043 --> 01:03:22.341
And I think he's
getting shaken up.

869
01:03:22.879 --> 01:03:24.904
Doesn't that sound like
an answered prayer?

870
01:03:25.081 --> 01:03:27.049
It sounds
like an answered prayer to me.

871
01:03:27.217 --> 01:03:29.811
But he's in serious trouble
right now, you know that?

872
01:03:30.086 --> 01:03:31.713
And he's
way over his head.

873
01:03:32.322 --> 01:03:33.346
- Okay.
- There.

874
01:03:34.491 --> 01:03:36.049
Are you sure
you wanna go in?

875
01:03:36.860 --> 01:03:38.157
You can wait here.

876
01:03:39.062 --> 01:03:40.086
I need to see.

877
01:04:03.019 --> 01:04:04.247
We're looking for a girl.

878
01:04:04.688 --> 01:04:05.712
Raj sent us.

879
01:04:06.122 --> 01:04:07.749
- You have money?
- Yeah.

880
01:04:08.091 --> 01:04:09.115
Please.

881
01:04:15.498 --> 01:04:17.830
- What about this?
- No.

882
01:04:21.271 --> 01:04:23.262
Don't waste my time.

883
01:04:23.607 --> 01:04:25.438
No, no, no,
I can get more money.

884
01:04:25.942 --> 01:04:28.740
lf you have the girl,
I'm telling you, cash is no problem.

885
01:04:30.614 --> 01:04:31.638
You want the girl?

886
01:04:31.848 --> 01:04:35.011
Is she here?
The one we asked Raj about?

887
01:04:35.318 --> 01:04:38.082
The same, the same.
lf you want to buy girls, give me this.

888
01:04:38.855 --> 01:04:39.879
- Give me!
- No, no!

889
01:04:41.958 --> 01:04:43.482
I need this one.

890
01:04:44.761 --> 01:04:45.955
This one for sure.

891
01:05:03.380 --> 01:05:05.211
I need the other one, okay?

892
01:05:05.382 --> 01:05:07.782
The one I just showed you.
The one in the picture.

893
01:05:08.485 --> 01:05:10.476
No, she's not here.
She had an accident.

894
01:05:10.820 --> 01:05:12.310
So, you want two?

895
01:05:14.891 --> 01:05:18.691
She's not here.
Look, I sell you. I have others.

896
01:05:19.062 --> 01:05:20.586
- You want to buy or not?
- Annikka!

897
01:05:20.764 --> 01:05:22.698
- What'd I say?
- Annikka!

898
01:05:27.637 --> 01:05:28.661
Listen to me, hey--

899
01:05:32.475 --> 01:05:33.499
Listen to me.

900
01:05:37.847 --> 01:05:41.078
I have told you, she has an accident.
She is not here.

901
01:05:41.651 --> 01:05:44.347
Just go get the other one.
I'll pay you whatever you want.

902
01:05:45.088 --> 01:05:46.112
- You want to buy?
- Yes.

903
01:05:46.489 --> 01:05:48.821
lf you have the other one, please,
get her quick.

904
01:05:48.992 --> 01:05:50.016
Come, come.

905
01:05:57.067 --> 01:05:58.091
Wait here.
Coming.

906
01:06:03.573 --> 01:06:04.597
Is she right?

907
01:06:07.310 --> 01:06:08.334
She is good?

908
01:06:11.181 --> 01:06:13.547
We need to pray about it.
We can't stop praying.

909
01:06:13.717 --> 01:06:15.082
- No.
- Let's pray right now.

910
01:06:15.251 --> 01:06:16.275
No way.
I'm done.

911
01:06:16.619 --> 01:06:18.678
- I'm not praying about this anymore.
- Okay?

912
01:06:18.855 --> 01:06:20.186
I prayed him into this mess.

913
01:06:20.357 --> 01:06:23.554
- Then I will pray about it.
- No, you know what? I'm done praying.

914
01:06:24.327 --> 01:06:26.659
That's what got
him there in the first place.

915
01:06:26.863 --> 01:06:28.262
Come on,
sweetheart.

916
01:06:28.998 --> 01:06:31.831
Your praying did not get him
in this mess in the first place.

917
01:06:32.001 --> 01:06:33.696
What got him into this mess...

918
01:06:33.870 --> 01:06:36.430
...was him deciding
he was going to man up.

919
01:06:36.906 --> 01:06:39.340
That's what got him in this
mess in the first place.

920
01:06:39.509 --> 01:06:42.672
- Yeah, but what if he doesn't man up?
- As far as I can see--

921
01:06:44.247 --> 01:06:45.612
You prayed that our son...

922
01:06:46.149 --> 01:06:49.084
...would start seeing the world
through different eyes.

923
01:06:49.419 --> 01:06:52.047
Start seeing other people
in different ways.

924
01:06:53.323 --> 01:06:55.314
And that's exactly
what's happening.

925
01:06:56.059 --> 01:06:57.083
Exactly.

926
01:06:57.861 --> 01:06:59.829
Yeah, but, you know,
he's so far away.

927
01:07:00.330 --> 01:07:03.891
And we're here
and he's feeling so bad...

928
01:07:04.701 --> 01:07:06.396
...and there's nothing
I can do.

929
01:07:06.569 --> 01:07:08.730
You're right,
there's nothing you can do.

930
01:07:08.938 --> 01:07:10.633
We're gonna pray.

931
01:07:11.274 --> 01:07:12.366
Come on.

932
01:07:13.576 --> 01:07:14.668
Come on.

933
01:07:20.717 --> 01:07:22.275
Dear God...

934
01:07:26.556 --> 01:07:29.150
...we thank you so much
for answering our prayers.

935
01:07:30.627 --> 01:07:33.790
We put our family
right there at your feet.

936
01:07:35.398 --> 01:07:39.027
Help us never to forget
that no matter how much I love my wife...

937
01:07:41.838 --> 01:07:43.863
...that you love her
even more.

938
01:07:45.141 --> 01:07:48.406
Also, no matter
how much my wife loves our son...

939
01:07:49.879 --> 01:07:52.541
...that you love him
even more.

940
01:07:55.518 --> 01:07:57.509
I thank you for the wonderful blessings...

941
01:07:57.720 --> 01:08:01.622
...you have bestowed upon me and
my family, and the responsibility...

942
01:08:01.991 --> 01:08:04.152
...that you've given
me and my family.

943
01:08:05.628 --> 01:08:07.289
We pray these prayers...

944
01:08:08.164 --> 01:08:10.189
...in the glorious name
of your son.

945
01:08:12.135 --> 01:08:13.159
Amen.

946
01:08:14.504 --> 01:08:15.528
Amen.

947
01:08:27.650 --> 01:08:28.878
I trusted you!

948
01:08:30.987 --> 01:08:32.284
You failed me again.

949
01:08:32.989 --> 01:08:34.650
Again. Again!

950
01:08:35.158 --> 01:08:36.921
- And again! And again!
- Please, please!

951
01:08:37.527 --> 01:08:38.551
Sir, stop!

952
01:08:40.697 --> 01:08:41.721
Sir, you did good.

953
01:08:43.433 --> 01:08:44.991
Sir, you saved
these girls.

954
01:08:48.438 --> 01:08:50.167
- It's good.
- Are you kidding me?

955
01:08:53.643 --> 01:08:54.667
I'm done with this.

956
01:08:55.278 --> 01:08:58.213
How many did we
leave behind?

957
01:08:58.948 --> 01:09:00.882
There is no good in this!

958
01:09:04.387 --> 01:09:06.651
You're spoiled, right?

959
01:09:07.790 --> 01:09:10.759
Everything always
given to you?

960
01:09:11.594 --> 01:09:12.618
You not fight?

961
01:09:14.264 --> 01:09:15.822
I know your God
is listening...

962
01:09:16.032 --> 01:09:18.466
...but not answer to you
like you want.

963
01:09:19.502 --> 01:09:22.596
So you run, hide, kick.

964
01:09:27.010 --> 01:09:28.204
Look at these kids.

965
01:09:29.078 --> 01:09:30.841
Look at these little girls.

966
01:09:32.882 --> 01:09:35.180
Their lives are ruined.

967
01:09:36.152 --> 01:09:37.744
They'll never forget this.

968
01:09:38.855 --> 01:09:41.653
You not forget,
we look for Annikka.

969
01:09:42.258 --> 01:09:43.816
She may be
in trouble out there.

970
01:09:44.093 --> 01:09:46.561
Let's remember
that you sold her.

971
01:09:47.497 --> 01:09:48.521
You sold her!

972
01:09:49.966 --> 01:09:53.231
And besides, who are you
to question me or my faith?

973
01:09:53.803 --> 01:09:56.636
Why not? You just
questioned the faith just now.

974
01:10:06.149 --> 01:10:08.617
When I was just little...

975
01:10:09.953 --> 01:10:13.480
...these white people
told me about your god, Jesus...

976
01:10:13.723 --> 01:10:19.218
...and said we create
in his image.

977
01:10:24.067 --> 01:10:27.264
Yeah, everybody
except us Dalits.

978
01:10:28.571 --> 01:10:30.562
I not know.
He--

979
01:10:31.608 --> 01:10:33.576
Not possible for me
to think this.

980
01:10:33.943 --> 01:10:35.638
He create me
and love me like this.

981
01:10:35.912 --> 01:10:38.107
But you have everything.

982
01:10:39.515 --> 01:10:42.040
Food, money, school.

983
01:10:44.253 --> 01:10:47.120
And I know I did that...

984
01:10:47.924 --> 01:10:50.791
...because I thought was best
for Annikka.

985
01:10:54.864 --> 01:10:56.126
I know.

986
01:10:58.901 --> 01:11:00.562
I'm sorry, I just--

987
01:11:01.270 --> 01:11:02.862
Look, I don't know...

988
01:11:04.040 --> 01:11:05.268
...how to live this way.

989
01:11:05.541 --> 01:11:07.805
I've never seen
anything like this before.

990
01:11:09.212 --> 01:11:12.545
I don't know how to be here.
I don't know how to live this way.

991
01:11:13.282 --> 01:11:14.306
Me either.

992
01:11:15.818 --> 01:11:18.651
This not my life.

993
01:11:21.491 --> 01:11:22.788
But you have to be happy...

994
01:11:22.992 --> 01:11:27.053
...with everything
you have today, now.

995
01:11:30.566 --> 01:11:32.761
I think you here
for this reason.

996
01:11:34.671 --> 01:11:36.070
Thank you.

997
01:12:15.478 --> 01:12:16.638
Come here,
listen to this.

998
01:12:19.515 --> 01:12:20.539
Yes?

999
01:12:21.150 --> 01:12:22.674
- Your mom?
- Yeah.

1000
01:12:24.253 --> 01:12:27.017
- This America?
- Yeah.

1001
01:12:28.024 --> 01:12:30.390
She says,
"I'm praying that God...

1002
01:12:30.560 --> 01:12:32.687
...will take you
out of your comfort zone...

1003
01:12:33.329 --> 01:12:34.853
...rattle you a little."

1004
01:12:39.902 --> 01:12:41.802
She also says
earlier that...

1005
01:12:42.705 --> 01:12:44.798
..."My prayer for you
is that you will see...

1006
01:12:44.974 --> 01:12:48.501
...what you have
and what others lack...

1007
01:12:50.713 --> 01:12:53.238
...and bridge that gap
with your heart."

1008
01:12:57.887 --> 01:12:59.320
Talk about faith.

1009
01:13:02.759 --> 01:13:04.021
So what do we do now?

1010
01:13:04.360 --> 01:13:06.624
- Find Annikka.
- Yeah.

1011
01:13:07.764 --> 01:13:11.825
I don't know what else to do.
We don't have any more information.

1012
01:13:12.068 --> 01:13:13.865
We don't have
any more maps.

1013
01:13:14.504 --> 01:13:16.369
All we have
is that note.

1014
01:13:19.008 --> 01:13:20.475
It doesn't even
say anything.

1015
01:13:24.981 --> 01:13:26.471
Just read it again.

1016
01:13:37.994 --> 01:13:39.256
What is that?

1017
01:13:40.663 --> 01:13:42.153
What is that?

1018
01:13:42.765 --> 01:13:44.164
- What?
- That.

1019
01:13:46.803 --> 01:13:48.430
Phone number.

1020
01:13:50.139 --> 01:13:51.504
It's a phone number?

1021
01:13:52.241 --> 01:13:53.674
Call it.

1022
01:13:57.914 --> 01:13:59.506
Call it.

1023
01:14:01.017 --> 01:14:03.417
Sir, I not use before this.

1024
01:14:05.254 --> 01:14:07.313
- Call.
- You've never used a phone before?

1025
01:14:07.590 --> 01:14:09.080
This number.

1026
01:14:16.098 --> 01:14:17.122
Yeah.

1027
01:14:19.268 --> 01:14:20.292
Hello?

1028
01:14:20.570 --> 01:14:22.037
- Hello.
- Hello?

1029
01:14:30.680 --> 01:14:31.942
- Hello?
- Hello?

1030
01:14:34.383 --> 01:14:35.407
Hello? Hello?

1031
01:14:35.785 --> 01:14:36.945
Just give me the phone.

1032
01:14:37.153 --> 01:14:38.211
- Hello?
- Hello?

1033
01:14:39.422 --> 01:14:40.582
Hey, do you
speak English?

1034
01:14:41.023 --> 01:14:42.047
Yes, sir.

1035
01:14:42.458 --> 01:14:43.925
Where are you
located?

1036
01:14:44.293 --> 01:14:46.989
Andheri West Laxmi
Industries.

1037
01:14:47.797 --> 01:14:50.061
I'm sorry, you have
to say that again.

1038
01:14:50.333 --> 01:14:53.063
Andheri West Laxmi
Industries.

1039
01:14:53.870 --> 01:14:55.895
Andheri West Laxmi.

1040
01:14:56.539 --> 01:14:58.370
Andheri West Laxmi....

1041
01:14:59.442 --> 01:15:01.501
Andheri West
at Laxmi Industry.

1042
01:15:02.278 --> 01:15:04.644
Andheri West
Laxmi Industry.

1043
01:15:05.715 --> 01:15:09.048
- Andheri West Laxmi Industry.
- Okay, thank you.

1044
01:15:10.052 --> 01:15:11.519
Andheri West Laxmi Industry.

1045
01:15:11.921 --> 01:15:13.218
Yeah, is it close?

1046
01:15:13.456 --> 01:15:14.946
I not know.

1047
01:15:17.593 --> 01:15:20.118
Come on, what do you mean,
you don't know?

1048
01:15:21.697 --> 01:15:23.528
We gotta go.
What do we do with them?

1049
01:15:24.800 --> 01:15:25.824
I--

1050
01:15:29.005 --> 01:15:30.029
I don't--

1051
01:15:30.206 --> 01:15:33.004
Do we gotta pick a straw
or something? I don't understand.

1052
01:15:33.576 --> 01:15:34.873
How do we get to this place?

1053
01:15:35.044 --> 01:15:37.877
- Andheri West Laxmi.
- Yes, how do we get there?

1054
01:15:39.248 --> 01:15:40.442
I not know.

1055
01:15:54.697 --> 01:15:56.528
Here you go, sir.
Anything else?

1056
01:15:56.866 --> 01:15:59.164
Thanks.
Yeah, actually.

1057
01:15:59.535 --> 01:16:01.901
I need to speak
to the manager or owner.

1058
01:16:03.706 --> 01:16:06.038
So what can l
do for you?

1059
01:16:06.842 --> 01:16:09.003
Actually, I'm looking
for a little girl...

1060
01:16:09.345 --> 01:16:12.781
...and I was told that the owner
would be able to help me.

1061
01:16:15.551 --> 01:16:19.647
Look, I'm looking
for a very specific girl.

1062
01:16:22.124 --> 01:16:23.682
Have you seen her?

1063
01:16:25.461 --> 01:16:26.860
Maybe yes.

1064
01:16:32.268 --> 01:16:33.599
How about now?

1065
01:16:34.070 --> 01:16:37.096
This is not the right
time and place for this.

1066
01:16:37.640 --> 01:16:38.937
You should follow me.

1067
01:16:39.208 --> 01:16:41.802
Can I have my wallet back?
Thanks.

1068
01:16:48.918 --> 01:16:51.614
Look, I can pay you
whatever you want...

1069
01:16:51.821 --> 01:16:53.288
...if you have this girl.

1070
01:16:53.656 --> 01:16:54.953
I can get you to her.

1071
01:16:55.291 --> 01:16:58.260
How much do you have
for fair price?

1072
01:17:00.796 --> 01:17:01.820
You tell me.

1073
01:17:03.632 --> 01:17:06.692
I would want
10 lakh rupees.

1074
01:17:07.203 --> 01:17:10.434
That means
one million rupees.

1075
01:17:13.442 --> 01:17:14.500
Yeah.

1076
01:17:15.444 --> 01:17:19.107
Wait, that's,
like, over $20,000.

1077
01:17:19.782 --> 01:17:22.250
lf you don't want her,
that's okay with me.

1078
01:17:22.551 --> 01:17:24.348
No, I do.
I--

1079
01:17:26.255 --> 01:17:27.654
I do, it's just--

1080
01:17:28.524 --> 01:17:31.459
lf I pay you,
I need that girl.

1081
01:17:32.294 --> 01:17:34.387
Okay? Not one like her.
Her.

1082
01:17:35.431 --> 01:17:37.228
Yes, she can be found.

1083
01:17:37.833 --> 01:17:39.630
But not by you.

1084
01:17:40.669 --> 01:17:43.263
I can get the money.
I need a few hours.

1085
01:17:44.106 --> 01:17:47.701
But not so long because I have
other customers as well, you see.

1086
01:17:50.446 --> 01:17:51.879
Please answer.

1087
01:17:53.482 --> 01:17:55.507
Dad. Dad. Dad.

1088
01:17:55.918 --> 01:17:57.408
Hey, no, it's me.

1089
01:17:57.920 --> 01:18:00.411
No, no,
you're breaking up really bad.

1090
01:18:01.257 --> 01:18:02.918
Hello? Hello?

1091
01:18:03.526 --> 01:18:05.494
Dad, yeah, listen.

1092
01:18:06.295 --> 01:18:08.388
Yes, I'm in India still.

1093
01:18:09.899 --> 01:18:11.867
Dad, I need
your help, okay?

1094
01:18:14.203 --> 01:18:17.502
I need a lot of money
and I need it really fast.

1095
01:18:18.974 --> 01:18:20.441
What? What?

1096
01:18:20.976 --> 01:18:23.570
Dad! Dad!

1097
01:18:36.292 --> 01:18:37.316
Please.

1098
01:18:39.095 --> 01:18:40.858
What am l
supposed to do now?

1099
01:18:41.330 --> 01:18:44.731
I need your help
right now.

1100
01:18:45.534 --> 01:18:47.525
Show me,
please, God.

1101
01:18:57.313 --> 01:18:58.746
Please, God.

1102
01:19:03.652 --> 01:19:04.676
I need your help.

1103
01:19:05.154 --> 01:19:07.816
I need--
I need your help right now.

1104
01:19:08.557 --> 01:19:10.923
Right now, right now.

1105
01:19:11.393 --> 01:19:12.792
Right now.

1106
01:19:15.631 --> 01:19:18.293
Please, please.
Right now.

1107
01:19:23.472 --> 01:19:24.837
Mom. Mom!

1108
01:19:25.040 --> 01:19:26.337
No, it's Luke.

1109
01:19:28.677 --> 01:19:30.167
- Is Mom there?
- Nape.

1110
01:19:30.613 --> 01:19:33.411
God put it on my heart to call you
to tell you that we're....

1111
01:19:33.716 --> 01:19:35.183
We're praying for you, son.

1112
01:19:35.451 --> 01:19:36.782
Thanks, Luke.

1113
01:19:37.219 --> 01:19:38.243
You doing okay?

1114
01:19:38.687 --> 01:19:40.814
No.
No, I'm not doing okay.

1115
01:19:40.990 --> 01:19:44.016
- I need a lot of money and I need it now.
- How much?

1116
01:19:44.760 --> 01:19:46.421
$20,000.

1117
01:19:47.963 --> 01:19:49.794
And I can't get
ahold of my dad.

1118
01:19:50.399 --> 01:19:51.661
Can I ask what for?

1119
01:19:51.901 --> 01:19:55.393
To buy a little girl back for her father,
if she's even still alive.

1120
01:19:56.305 --> 01:19:58.034
Okay, Luke,
this is bad.

1121
01:19:58.440 --> 01:20:00.431
Not, like, at home bad.

1122
01:20:00.776 --> 01:20:02.437
This is literally
life or death bad.

1123
01:20:02.711 --> 01:20:04.838
I know this is
not what you want to hear...

1124
01:20:05.014 --> 01:20:07.847
...but if you buy her back,
you'll hurt other little kids.

1125
01:20:08.017 --> 01:20:10.577
There's a reason why
we don't buy hostages back.

1126
01:20:11.487 --> 01:20:13.546
I'm guessing you went
to the police already?

1127
01:20:13.722 --> 01:20:17.214
Kiran said that they wouldn't care.
Or worse, we'd have to pay them, too.

1128
01:20:17.493 --> 01:20:19.290
- Kiran?
- The little girl's father.

1129
01:20:19.495 --> 01:20:22.259
Can your mother and I make some calls?
Where are you, son?

1130
01:20:22.565 --> 01:20:24.692
Luke, I don't
know where I am.

1131
01:20:25.401 --> 01:20:27.528
I'm somewhere
in Mumbai.

1132
01:20:28.237 --> 01:20:30.102
I met with this girl
at a restaurant.

1133
01:20:30.472 --> 01:20:35.000
She's here. The little girl's here.
It's all lined up. Luke, I need the money.

1134
01:20:35.611 --> 01:20:38.079
lf we don't find her now,
we may never be able to.

1135
01:20:38.247 --> 01:20:40.238
I didn't say
I wouldn't send the money...

1136
01:20:40.416 --> 01:20:44.853
...but I do believe that God
will make a better way, Caden.

1137
01:20:45.087 --> 01:20:47.885
I need to tell you,
I am so proud of what you're doing.

1138
01:20:48.057 --> 01:20:51.857
I can't imagine in my wildest dreams
what's happening there, but I believe...

1139
01:20:52.027 --> 01:20:54.757
...God will make a way
that won't hurt kids. I know that.

1140
01:20:54.930 --> 01:20:56.921
God's not
making a way, Luke.

1141
01:20:58.167 --> 01:21:01.068
lf he is, I'm really stupid
or just plain blind.

1142
01:21:01.370 --> 01:21:03.395
No, you are not stupid,
you're scared.

1143
01:21:03.572 --> 01:21:04.664
Who wouldn't be scared?

1144
01:21:04.873 --> 01:21:06.568
Now, where should
I wire the money?

1145
01:21:08.110 --> 01:21:09.577
Luke, come on.

1146
01:21:10.246 --> 01:21:13.079
I know you don't have
that kind of money just laying around.

1147
01:21:13.249 --> 01:21:15.717
You're right, I don't.
Where can I get it to you?

1148
01:21:15.918 --> 01:21:19.684
I'll get it to you as fast as I can.
It might take an hour, it might take two.

1149
01:21:19.855 --> 01:21:21.550
But in the meantime,
can I ask you...

1150
01:21:21.724 --> 01:21:25.455
...to please think hard and pray about this
before you do anything?

1151
01:21:25.728 --> 01:21:27.423
No. Okay, just...

1152
01:21:28.163 --> 01:21:29.790
...please wire the money?

1153
01:21:30.299 --> 01:21:33.427
Send it to a Western Union
near the Taj Hotel.

1154
01:21:35.704 --> 01:21:37.069
I think that's where I'm at.

1155
01:21:37.373 --> 01:21:40.809
I'm sorry, that's all the information I have,
so I hope it's enough.

1156
01:21:41.076 --> 01:21:43.135
Okay,
Western Union.

1157
01:21:43.812 --> 01:21:46.110
Caden, you hang
in there, son.

1158
01:21:46.582 --> 01:21:48.140
I'm gonna get
that money to--

1159
01:21:53.656 --> 01:21:54.680
Dear God.

1160
01:21:56.759 --> 01:21:57.783
Please.

1161
01:22:19.281 --> 01:22:20.305
No!

1162
01:22:28.724 --> 01:22:30.157
Sir, what happened?

1163
01:22:35.631 --> 01:22:36.655
Sir?

1164
01:22:37.232 --> 01:22:38.597
Where's Annikka?

1165
01:22:39.735 --> 01:22:41.202
Where are the girls?

1166
01:22:43.672 --> 01:22:44.696
They go.

1167
01:22:45.407 --> 01:22:46.897
What do you mean,
"they go"?

1168
01:22:47.276 --> 01:22:48.300
Where did they go?

1169
01:22:49.111 --> 01:22:51.978
Sir, I went to get food,
you no come back,

1170
01:22:52.247 --> 01:22:54.715
And I came,
they going.

1171
01:22:55.084 --> 01:22:57.450
I said, "Where to go?"
They said, "Back."

1172
01:22:58.153 --> 01:23:00.087
They went.
Now we find Annikka?

1173
01:23:02.057 --> 01:23:03.081
Sir, please?

1174
01:23:03.525 --> 01:23:04.924
How is that possible?

1175
01:23:05.260 --> 01:23:07.023
Why would you
let them do that?

1176
01:23:07.396 --> 01:23:08.988
Sir, these girl big.

1177
01:23:09.365 --> 01:23:12.459
They could have baby, husband.
They not listen to me.

1178
01:23:12.668 --> 01:23:15.159
Are you telling me
that they--

1179
01:23:15.471 --> 01:23:17.666
They choose
to live like that?

1180
01:23:17.906 --> 01:23:19.339
Sir.

1181
01:23:20.409 --> 01:23:23.674
Sir, if their father
Dalit...

1182
01:23:24.613 --> 01:23:27.639
...they tell the girl
they not good, they mistake.

1183
01:23:28.951 --> 01:23:31.044
Not worth nothing.

1184
01:23:32.054 --> 01:23:33.521
That is so jacked up.

1185
01:23:43.799 --> 01:23:44.823
Sir.

1186
01:23:52.274 --> 01:23:54.105
Hey, I thought
you changed your mind.

1187
01:23:54.443 --> 01:23:55.467
No.

1188
01:23:56.044 --> 01:23:59.445
No, no, no, I went
to go get the money.

1189
01:24:00.215 --> 01:24:01.944
It's here,
it's on its way.

1190
01:24:02.251 --> 01:24:03.650
We just have to go get it.

1191
01:24:04.353 --> 01:24:06.253
- Do you know him?
- Yes, yes, yes.

1192
01:24:06.588 --> 01:24:07.612
He's with me.

1193
01:24:13.028 --> 01:24:15.724
You know, his kind
is not fit for the city.

1194
01:24:15.931 --> 01:24:17.831
Oh, come on.
What does his kind matter?

1195
01:24:18.500 --> 01:24:20.627
You're about to make money off of me.

1196
01:24:20.803 --> 01:24:22.794
What does his kind
have to do with anything?

1197
01:24:24.807 --> 01:24:27.002
But he is not going
to come with us.

1198
01:24:27.509 --> 01:24:29.306
I need to take
another cab.

1199
01:24:31.513 --> 01:24:33.640
lf anything happens to him,
the deal's off.

1200
01:24:44.059 --> 01:24:45.617
I'm here
to pick up some money.

1201
01:24:45.928 --> 01:24:46.952
Can I have your ID?

1202
01:25:14.790 --> 01:25:16.417
Hey, where's my friend?

1203
01:25:17.059 --> 01:25:18.356
He is coming, no problem.

1204
01:25:18.727 --> 01:25:20.319
Do you want the girl or not?

1205
01:25:20.829 --> 01:25:22.490
You want to waste
some more time?

1206
01:25:22.698 --> 01:25:24.427
Maybe she
already spoken for.

1207
01:25:35.377 --> 01:25:37.937
Come on, let's go.
Once we get in, you can pick.

1208
01:25:38.480 --> 01:25:40.778
What? No, no.

1209
01:25:40.949 --> 01:25:44.180
That wasn't the deal. I told you
who I wanted. You said she was there.

1210
01:25:44.520 --> 01:25:45.544
Yes, I know.

1211
01:25:45.888 --> 01:25:48.083
I thought you changed
your mind like the others.

1212
01:25:48.524 --> 01:25:49.548
Come on, get out.

1213
01:26:48.216 --> 01:26:49.774
She's not in here.

1214
01:26:51.753 --> 01:26:53.118
Wait, wait,
I have more.

1215
01:27:52.714 --> 01:27:54.409
Please tell me
you have more.

1216
01:27:54.750 --> 01:27:56.342
Well, these are
my best girls.

1217
01:27:56.518 --> 01:27:58.986
You can pick the one
which makes you happy.

1218
01:28:01.089 --> 01:28:02.351
No, no, no.

1219
01:28:03.692 --> 01:28:04.716
I've showed you.

1220
01:28:04.893 --> 01:28:06.861
I want this one
right here, you see?

1221
01:28:13.335 --> 01:28:14.359
Who said that?

1222
01:28:15.937 --> 01:28:17.768
- Where is she?
- Oh, that one?

1223
01:28:18.073 --> 01:28:20.564
She's not good.
She always ask for some dollies...

1224
01:28:20.776 --> 01:28:22.073
...some puppet
or something.

1225
01:28:22.277 --> 01:28:23.938
- She's just worthless.
- Where is she?

1226
01:28:24.312 --> 01:28:27.475
I told you, you don't want that.
These are my best girls.

1227
01:28:28.183 --> 01:28:30.048
Never mind, okay?

1228
01:28:30.786 --> 01:28:32.981
I know she's in here.
I don't need your help.

1229
01:28:37.959 --> 01:28:39.119
Who said that?

1230
01:28:47.636 --> 01:28:50.537
I want her. That's the one.
I have the money. I'll pay.

1231
01:28:50.706 --> 01:28:51.730
She's not my best.

1232
01:28:51.940 --> 01:28:53.271
That's the one
I came for.

1233
01:29:10.358 --> 01:29:11.655
You know what?

1234
01:29:14.663 --> 01:29:19.225
No money will ever fix what you're doing
to these little girls.

1235
01:29:19.668 --> 01:29:21.158
So I'm taking her, okay?

1236
01:29:21.436 --> 01:29:23.529
And I promise,
I will be back to get the rest.

1237
01:29:23.705 --> 01:29:24.729
Come here.

1238
01:29:25.140 --> 01:29:26.164
Get off!

1239
01:29:26.341 --> 01:29:27.365
Hey, get off!

1240
01:30:01.643 --> 01:30:02.667
Annikka!

1241
01:30:03.278 --> 01:30:05.542
Annikka!

1242
01:31:40.709 --> 01:31:42.540
Turns out,
when Luke said he and Mom...

1243
01:31:42.711 --> 01:31:45.509
...would make some calls,
he meant it.

1244
01:31:48.316 --> 01:31:51.046
Not For Sale.
That was the first call they made.

1245
01:31:51.319 --> 01:31:52.343
NFS.

1246
01:31:52.654 --> 01:31:55.555
A set of initials that a few weeks ago
meant nothing to me.

1247
01:31:56.057 --> 01:31:59.049
But now they're names
and people I will never forget.

1248
01:32:01.429 --> 01:32:04.728
As I look at this little girl,
damaged by whatever happened...

1249
01:32:05.033 --> 01:32:06.660
...I didn't have
the guts to ask...

1250
01:32:07.068 --> 01:32:09.866
...but based on what
the NFS people said...

1251
01:32:11.473 --> 01:32:13.373
...it breaks my heart
to even imagine.

1252
01:32:16.244 --> 01:32:18.735
And her father,
trying to make it all better.

1253
01:32:19.547 --> 01:32:22.175
I know neither one of them
will ever be the same.

1254
01:32:22.951 --> 01:32:25.044
All I can think about
are the other kids...

1255
01:32:25.253 --> 01:32:26.811
...who are being kept
as slaves...

1256
01:32:27.055 --> 01:32:30.456
...away from home, away from
the people they love and who love them.

1257
01:32:34.095 --> 01:32:36.086
Now that's
what haunts me.

1258
01:32:40.368 --> 01:32:41.926
There is something
to that saying.

1259
01:32:42.304 --> 01:32:44.534
"I once was lost,
but now I'm found. "

1260
01:32:45.340 --> 01:32:46.364
It's true.

1261
01:32:47.409 --> 01:32:48.740
I feel it.

1262
01:32:53.481 --> 01:32:55.676
As for my prize
possessions....

1263
01:32:56.718 --> 01:32:59.516
I have to say,
it is nice to have my camera back.

1264
01:33:00.388 --> 01:33:03.755
And my watch. Trading it
for that little girl...

1265
01:33:03.959 --> 01:33:06.757
...even if she did end up
running back. It was worth it.

1266
01:33:10.699 --> 01:33:13.725
It seems easy to see that
the hand of God was guiding...

1267
01:33:14.169 --> 01:33:15.693
...because now I'm aware.

1268
01:33:17.172 --> 01:33:18.662
I have no more excuses...

1269
01:33:18.873 --> 01:33:22.969
...and the very least I can do
is get involved.

1270
01:33:58.413 --> 01:34:02.349
Human trafficking is a problem worldwide
that affects each and every one of us.

1271
01:34:02.584 --> 01:34:06.350
It has been our goal as storytellers
to try and start a global conversation.

1272
01:34:06.554 --> 01:34:10.149
To get people talking about trafficking,
sex slavery, and the Dalits of India.

1273
01:34:10.358 --> 01:34:12.849
It's everyone's issue,
and should be everyone's cause.

1274
01:34:13.061 --> 01:34:15.552
I'm Brent Martz,
producer of Not Today.

1275
01:34:15.797 --> 01:34:17.628
- I'm Cody Longo.
- I'm Cassie Scerbo.

1276
01:34:17.799 --> 01:34:18.959
My name is Walid Amini.

1277
01:34:19.167 --> 01:34:20.293
I'm Shari Rigby.

1278
01:34:20.468 --> 01:34:23.062
I want to personally
thank you for supporting this film.

1279
01:34:23.338 --> 01:34:25.636
Human trafficking
is a huge issue worldwide.

1280
01:34:25.840 --> 01:34:28.035
A problem that affects
every one of us.

1281
01:34:28.276 --> 01:34:32.212
We made Not Today in India because
we've been working here for 10 years.

1282
01:34:32.414 --> 01:34:35.747
We chose to make it here because
it's an amazing and beautiful country.

1283
01:34:35.917 --> 01:34:38.545
Because of these kids,
these faces you're seeing.

1284
01:34:38.753 --> 01:34:41.847
I had no idea that right now, today,
there are more than--

1285
01:34:42.090 --> 01:34:43.853
There are more
than 27 million--

1286
01:34:44.059 --> 01:34:45.083
27 million--

1287
01:34:45.293 --> 01:34:46.760
People enslaved
around the world.

1288
01:34:46.995 --> 01:34:49.964
I didn't know that children
as young as 4 and 5 years old...

1289
01:34:50.131 --> 01:34:52.099
...are bought and sold
for sex daily.

1290
01:34:52.333 --> 01:34:55.860
And I also didn't know about
the Dalits of India. The untouchables.

1291
01:34:56.104 --> 01:34:59.835
A group of nearly 300 million people
who are abused and degraded.

1292
01:35:00.008 --> 01:35:04.001
Because of where they are born.
Their last names, the color of their skin.

1293
01:35:04.312 --> 01:35:07.543
You might recognize this girl here
from the movie you just watched.

1294
01:35:07.949 --> 01:35:11.441
Her real name is Persis Karen,
but she played Annikka in the movie.

1295
01:35:11.753 --> 01:35:14.813
She's only here because someone
like you decided to get involved.

1296
01:35:15.056 --> 01:35:18.617
Now I'm aware, and now, for me,
doing nothing is not an option.

1297
01:35:18.860 --> 01:35:20.384
I hope you feel
the same way.

1298
01:35:20.595 --> 01:35:22.688
lf you do, together we can make
a difference.

1299
01:35:22.864 --> 01:35:27.062
Get out your phones and text the word
"today" to the number on your screen.

1300
01:35:27.268 --> 01:35:30.567
We'll send you a link to a website that'll
offer ways to get involved.

1301
01:35:30.772 --> 01:35:33.297
Helping to build a school,
sponsoring children.

1302
01:35:33.541 --> 01:35:36.669
Or volunteer your time
to a worthwhile organization...

1303
01:35:36.945 --> 01:35:38.708
...who desperately
needs your support.

1304
01:35:38.913 --> 01:35:41.381
To us, how you get involved
is not important.

1305
01:35:41.549 --> 01:35:44.074
What is important
is that you do get involved.

1306
01:35:44.285 --> 01:35:47.015
By texting the word "today"
to the number on your screen...

1307
01:35:47.188 --> 01:35:51.249
...you'll be able to make a difference in
the lives of kids like these.

1308
01:35:51.526 --> 01:35:54.927
Text the word "today" to the number on
the screen and watch what happens.

1309
01:35:55.163 --> 01:35:56.562
Watch what happens next.

1310
01:35:57.031 --> 01:35:58.328
You'll be glad you did.

1311
01:35:58.733 --> 01:35:59.757
So join us.

1312
01:36:00.101 --> 01:36:03.002
Together we can provide freedom
to children around the world...

1313
01:36:03.204 --> 01:36:05.570
...and to see the end
of human trafficking.
